,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.866913621,"data":"       | Given f: Z_12 -\u003e {0,1}, define g(d) = d + 1 if f(d)=0, else d - 1 if f(d)=1. So g is essentially a \"signed shift\" where each position either moves forward or backward by 1. This is reminiscent of a \"signed permutation\" known as a \"signed shift\" generating a permutation with cycles of length maybe 2? Let's examine small examples.\n"}
