,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.868426435,"data":"       | Thus there are two types of cycles: one where first hand moves n times (i.e., a'=1) and second hand moves n^2 - n times; and the opposite where first hand moves n^2 - n times (a'=n-1). Since the two hands are distinguishable? The problem says two hands can move independently; they are distinct (hour and minute? Actually analog clock with two hands). The sequence of moves picks which hand moves each step. So swapping roles yields distinct sequences. So both a' values count.\n"}
