,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.869110252,"data":"       | analysisFor n=6, total moves =36. E counts possible: 6,30. That's a'=1 or 5 (n-1). So only extremes. So pattern: For even n, only a'=1 or n-1 are possible; for odd n, all a' from 1 to n-1 possible? Let's test n=7 maybe using backtracking? 49 vertices, may be huge. But maybe pattern emerges: For odd n, there are many possibilities.\n"}
