,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.869598297,"data":"       | Case 1: all zeros (d_k = 0 for all k). Then rule: if d_δ=0, we move east (increment i). So for any vertex, we always move east. Thus the permutation T(i,j) = (i+1, j) for all (i,j). This is a translation by (1,0) on torus. The order of this permutation is 12 (since after 12 east moves, i returns to original, j unchanged). Actually after 12 steps, (i,j) -\u003e (i+12, j) = (i,j). So the permutation decomposes into 12 cycles each of length 12? Wait each j coordinate is invariant, i cycles through 12 positions. So there are 12 cycles (one for each j). So not a single 144-cycle. So this pattern does NOT meet requirement.\n"}
