,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.87002531,"data":"       | Counting such permutations is reminiscent of counting \"Hamiltonian cycles in the directed grid graph D_{n,m}\" where each vertex has outdegree 2 (east and north). I recall known results: number of Hamiltonian cycles in an n×n toroidal grid with moves east and north is given by something like (2^n + 2^m - 2)?? Not sure.\n"}
