,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.871341974,"data":"       | Thus for n=4, the sequences are exactly all words w of length 4 that contain at least one A and at least one B, repeated n times = 4 repeats. But there are 2^4 - 2 = 14 such words, but we only have 8 sequences. So why not all? Let's see which patterns missing: length 4 words with both letters: there are 14. Which ones appear? The list includes patterns with exactly one B (AAA B) and patterns with exactly one A (BBB A) and patterns with 2 As and 2 Bs maybe? Let's check: pattern \"A A B B\"? Not present. \"A B A B\"? Not present. \"A B B A\"? Not present. \"B A A B\"? Not present. \"B A B A\"? Not present. \"B B A A\"? Not present. So patterns with 2 As and 2 Bs are missing. So only patterns with 1 of one letter and 3 of the other appear (i.e., 4 patterns per each letter? Actually patterns with 1 B (3 As) there are 4 distinct rotations (positions of B) =\u003e 4 patterns. Similarly 1 A (3 Bs) gives 4 patterns. Total 8 patterns, matching enumeration. So patterns with equal numbers (2 As,2 Bs) are not allowed for n=4.\n"}
