,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873127906,"data":"       | analysisOk.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873129016,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873130098,"data":"       | Now we need N for n=12. That's huge. We must find general formula.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873131303,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873132411,"data":"       | Observation: The directed graph is a \"directed torus\" where each vertex has out-degree 2 and in-degree 2. Hamiltonian cycles correspond to \"Eulerian trails\" of something? Perhaps they correspond to \"de Bruijn sequences of order 2 over alphabet of size n\"? Let's analyze that connection.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873134217,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873135348,"data":"       | Define each vertex (i,j). Edge east (increment i) corresponds to moving from (i,j) to (i+1,j). Edge north corresponds to moving from (i,j) to (i,j+1). Consider labeling edges by something maybe.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873136801,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873137901,"data":"       | If we consider mapping (i,j) -\u003e i (first coordinate). Then moving east increments i, moving north keeps i same. Similarly for j.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873139235,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873140325,"data":"       | Now think of sequence of moves as a string over alphabet {E,N}. Starting at (0,0), after t steps we have i = number of E moves, j = t - number of E moves. So visited vertices correspond to pairs (E count modulo n, (t - E count) modulo n). As earlier.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873141849,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873142943,"data":"       | Now condition for distinctness: For each residue t mod n, the set of (E count mod n) across the n times with that residue must be a permutation.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.87314431,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873145671,"data":"       | Thus we can think of constructing an n x n array A where rows correspond to residue r (t mod n) and columns correspond to step index within that residue (k = floor(t / n)). Actually t = r + n*k. Then a_{r,k} = h(t) = f(t) mod n = number of E moves up to time t mod n. The condition that for each r, the values a_{r,k} for k=0..n-1 are a permutation of Z_n.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873147417,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873148477,"data":"       | Now we also have monotonic condition across t. Let's examine how a_{r,k} relate across k.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873149719,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873150799,"data":"       | Observe that t increases by 1 each step. When we go from t to t+1, either we increment f(t) (if step is E) or keep same (if N). So h(t+1) = h(t) or h(t)+1 (mod n) depending.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873152223,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873153303,"data":"       | Consider the representation in matrix of size n x n (rows r, columns k). The ordering of t in row-major order: t = r + n*k (k from 0..n-1). For each row, as we move across columns (increase k by 1, which adds n steps), h(t) may change multiple times (since within n steps you may have many A steps). But we can analyze pattern.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873156655,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873157798,"data":"       | Instead, think of constructing a \"Latin square\" of order n: define L(r,c) = a_{r,c}, the value of f(r + n*c) mod n. Requirement: For each fixed r, the list over c is a permutation (i.e., each symbol appears exactly once). Additionally, the monotonic condition across t (which traverses by rows?) imposes that as we increment t by 1 (which moves within row, column order: first row r=0, column c from 0..n-1, then row r=1? Wait t enumerates in natural order, not row-major: t increments by 1, which increments r (mod n) while possibly incrementing column when r wraps from n-1 to 0. So t sequence goes through residues r in order: 0,1,2,...,n-1,0,1,2,... repeating. That is column-major order: each \"full cycle\" of n steps increments the column index c by 1 and resets r.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873160347,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873161467,"data":"       | Thus t = r + n*c where r cycles fastest (inner loop), c increments after each n steps. So as we progress, we move through rows cyclically, column index increments after each n steps.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873162893,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873164206,"data":"       | Hence the condition that for each fixed row r, the values across columns (c) form a permutation, as earlier.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873165487,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.87316657,"data":"       | Now monotonic condition across t: when we move from t to t+1, r increases by 1 (mod n). The column c stays same unless r wraps from n-1 to 0, then c increments by 1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873168033,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873169106,"data":"       | Thus the sequence of h(t) values along t is: h_{0,0}, h_{1,0}, ..., h_{n-1,0}, h_{0,1}, h_{1,1},..., h_{n-1,1}, etc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873170405,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873171502,"data":"       | The rule: h_{r+1,c} = h_{r,c} or h_{r,c}+1 (mod n) when r+1 \u003c n; and when r=n-1 and we go to r=0, column increases (c+1), we have h_{0,c+1} = h_{n-1,c} or h_{n-1,c}+1 (mod n) as well (since step increments either A or N). So same rule across wrap.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873173097,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873174163,"data":"       | Thus across each column, the values as we go down rows must be nondecreasing modulo n with increments of at most 1 at each step (wrap modulo n). So for each column, the sequence of h values as we go down rows from r=0 to n-1 must be a \"path\" that increments by 0 or 1 (mod n) each step.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873175867,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873177088,"data":"       | Additionally, across column transition (from last row r=n-1 to first row of next column), the same rule applies: step is still either A (increment) or N (no increment), but note that after we move from (i,j) where j increased? Actually moving from t = n-1 + n*c (row n-1) to t+1 = 0 + n*(c+1) (row 0 of next column) corresponds to a step where we increment the second coordinate (since moving from r=n-1 to 0 resets row, and column increments). Let's see: the step from t to t+1 is always a move of type either increment x (A) or increment y (B). In our representation, moving from (r,c) to (r+1,c) (or to (0,c+1) when r=n-1) corresponds to a step; we need to decide which type of move each step corresponds to, based on whether h increments. Actually if the step is A (increment x), then h(t+1) = h(t)+1 (mod n) because number of A's increases by 1; else if step is B, h(t+1) = h(t). So the increment of h indicates which hand moved.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873180996,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873182245,"data":"       | Thus we can view the sequence of moves as exactly the sequence of increments of h across the traversal order of (r,c). The rule is: For each successive t, h either stays same or increments by 1 (mod n). No other changes.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873183757,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873184832,"data":"       | Thus we need to count number of matrices H of size n×n (rows r, columns c) with entries in Z_n such that:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873186184,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873187303,"data":"       | 1. For each row r, the multiset {H[r,c] : c=0..n-1} is a permutation of Z_n (i.e., each symbol appears exactly once in each row). (Row condition.)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873188683,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873189753,"data":"       | 2. For each column c, the sequence H[0,c], H[1,c], ..., H[n-1,c] satisfies that successive entries differ by either 0 or +1 (mod n). i.e., H[r+1,c] - H[r,c] ∈ {0,1} (mod n) for r=0..n-2. Also for transition from H[n-1,c] to H[0,c+1], we must have H[0,c+1] - H[n-1,c] ∈ {0,1} (mod n). (Column transition condition.)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873191487,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873192571,"data":"       | 3. Starting value H[0,0] = 0 (since at t=0, f=0). Also final condition after full traversal of all n^2 steps returns to start automatically if counts satisfy multiples of n (which will happen automatically due to row permutations maybe). But we need H[0,0]=0 ensures start.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873194171,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873195248,"data":"       | Now we need to count number of such matrices H (or equivalently sequences). This may be easier.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873196523,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873197588,"data":"       | Observe that condition (1) means each row is a permutation; condition (2) restricts how permutations vary across rows.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873198924,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873200036,"data":"       | Think of representing each column as a sequence of n entries that is a \"nondecreasing walk\" modulo n (i.e., each step increase by 0 or 1). Over n steps, the total increase from start to end (i.e., H[n-1,c] - H[0,c]) can be any value between 0 and n-1 depending on number of increments along column. Similarly across columns, the transition must also be 0 or 1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873201835,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873203143,"data":"       | If we think modulo n, a nondecreasing walk with steps 0 or 1 cannot wrap around unless we exceed n-1 increments. Since there are n steps, maximum total increase is n (if every step increments). But increase is modulo n, so could wrap to 0 if total increase = n (i.e., all steps increment). So allowed total increase per column (including final wrap to next column) may be any integer between 0 and n inclusive? Let's analyze.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873205003,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873206127,"data":"       | For a given column c, we have H[0,c] some value. Then for r from 0 to n-2, each step we can stay or increase by 1. So after n-1 steps within column we have H[n-1,c] = H[0,c] + s_c (mod n), where s_c is number of increments among those n-1 steps (0 ≤ s_c ≤ n-1). Then we go to H[0,c+1] (next column) with condition that H[0,c+1] = H[n-1,c] + t_c (mod n) where t_c ∈ {0,1} (increment if the step from last row to next column is A). So overall, from start of column c to start of column c+1, total increase = s_c + t_c (mod n). Since s_c in [0,n-1] and t_c in {0,1}. So total increase ∈ [0,n] (mod n). If s_c = n-1 and t_c =1, total increase = n (≡0 mod n). So it's possible to have wrap-around (i.e., total increase ≡0) if all steps increment (i.e., s_c = n-1 and t_c =1) or s_c =0 and t_c=0? Actually total increase 0 mod n can also happen if s_c =0 and t_c=0 (i.e., no increments in column and no increment at transition). Many possibilities.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873210468,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873211589,"data":"       | Now, row condition: each row must be a permutation. That means for each fixed r, across columns c, the values H[r,c] must be all distinct modulo n.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873212985,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873214083,"data":"       | Given the constraints, this seems related to \"complete mappings\" of cyclic groups; a complete mapping is a permutation σ of group G such that the function x → x + σ(x) is also a permutation. Might be relevant: Because we can think of mapping of columns to values per row.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.87321579,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873216856,"data":"       | Let's examine row r: values across columns are H[r,c]. The condition that each row is a permutation of Z_n means that for each fixed r, the map c → H[r,c] is a permutation.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873218294,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873219378,"data":"       | Now consider the differences between rows: Since H[r+1,c] - H[r,c] ∈ {0,1} (mod n) for each column (except when r = n-1 and next column). This suggests that each column's entries form a \"weakly increasing\" sequence.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873220997,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873222235,"data":"       | Thus perhaps we can think of constructing permutations column by column such that each successive row differs by at most +1 (mod n). That strongly restricts possibilities.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873223651,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873224731,"data":"       | Let's try to enumerate for small n using algorithmic enumeration of matrices H abiding by these constraints and see if counts match earlier N values. That will also help see pattern to extrapolate to n=12. For n=2..5 we have counts; we can compute counts via matrix enumeration for verification.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873226353,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873227453,"data":"       | We'll implement backtracking constructing matrix row by row or column by column. Use constraints: each row must be a permutation; each column must obey monotonic step condition.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.87322893,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873229997,"data":"       | Let's code for n up to maybe 6 to verify counts match earlier sequence.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873231243,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.87323233,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codedef count_H_matrices(n):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873233529,"data":"       |     # Backtrack column by column (or row by row)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873234701,"data":"       |     # We'll store matrix as list of lists H[r][c]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873235905,"data":"       |     # We'll enforce row permutation as we fill.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873237068,"data":"       |     # We'll fill entries in order of t: row-major (r cycles fastest)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873239791,"data":"       |     # Equivalent to original sequence.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873241017,"data":"       |     total = 0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873242126,"data":"       |     # Precompute set of all symbols\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873243278,"data":"       |     symbols = set(range(n))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873244414,"data":"       |     # Initialize rows with empty sets of used symbols\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873245623,"data":"       |     row_used = [set() for _ in range(n)]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873246862,"data":"       |     # We'll maintain previous entry in column to enforce step condition.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873248079,"data":"       |     # We'll fill column by column.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873249231,"data":"       |     def backtrack(col, prev_col_last_vals):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873250412,"data":"       |         # prev_col_last_vals is list of values H[n-1, col-1] for previous column (or None for first column)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873251708,"data":"       |         nonlocal total\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873252865,"data":"       |         if col == n:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873253981,"data":"       |             # all columns filled, need to check final wrap condition from last column to first column (col 0)?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873255274,"data":"       |             # Actually need condition from H[n-1, n-1] to H[0,0] (already 0). This condition should already be enforced when we filled column n-1? Not yet, because we need to consider transition from last column to first column (wrap) where step also must be 0 or 1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873257114,"data":"       |             # We'll check this at end.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873258315,"data":"       |             # Ensure that transition from last column's last row to first column first row is allowed:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873259603,"data":"       |             last_val = prev_col_last_vals[-1]  # value at H[n-1, n-1]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873260823,"data":"       |             first_val = 0  # H[0,0] fixed\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873261994,"data":"       |             diff = (first_val - last_val) % n\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873263162,"data":"       |             if diff not in (0,1):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873264321,"data":"       |                 return\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873265439,"data":"       |             # Also need to ensure that each row is permutation, already ensured.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873266671,"data":"       |             total += 1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873267783,"data":"       |             return\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873268895,"data":"       |         # Build column col values row by row\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.87327005,"data":"       |         # We'll use recursion over rows\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873271229,"data":"       |         col_vals = [None]*n\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873272343,"data":"       |         def fill_row(r, prev_val):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873273479,"data":"       |             # prev_val is value at previous row in same column (or None for r=0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873274709,"data":"       |             if r == n:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873275916,"data":"       |                 # column completed; need to check transition from previous column's last row to this column's first row\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873278737,"data":"       |                 # The condition for transition from previous column (col-1) last row to current column first row:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873280038,"data":"       |                 if col == 0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.87328121,"data":"       |                     # This is first column; previous column is last column (wrap). We'll handle later after whole matrix?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873282558,"data":"       |                     # Actually need condition from H[n-1, n-1] to H[0,0] which we handle at end.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.87328382,"data":"       |                     pass\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873284964,"data":"       |                 else:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873286115,"data":"       |                     # prev_col_last_vals is list of previous column's last row values (length col)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873287428,"data":"       |                     # For transition from H[n-1, col-1] = prev_col_last_vals[col-1] to H[0,col] = col_vals[0]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873288709,"data":"       |                     diff = (col_vals[0] - prev_col_last_vals[col-1]) % n\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873289925,"data":"       |                     if diff not in (0,1):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873291089,"data":"       |                         return\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873292213,"data":"       |                 # Now proceed to next column\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873293377,"data":"       |                 # Append this column's last value to list for future transitions\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873294783,"data":"       |                 backtrack(col+1, prev_col_last_vals + [col_vals[-1]])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873296004,"data":"       |                 return\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873297189,"data":"       |             # Determine possible values for H[r,col]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873298369,"data":"       |             # Must not have been used already in this row\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873299548,"data":"       |             used = row_used[r]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.87330074,"data":"       |             # For step condition: if r\u003e0, diff = col_vals[r] - col_vals[r-1] must be 0 or 1 mod n\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873302031,"data":"       |             # So possible values are those not used and satisfying diff condition.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873303277,"data":"       |             candidates = []\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.87330441,"data":"       |             if r == 0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873305524,"data":"       |                 # No previous row in same column\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873306786,"data":"       |                 # Any unused symbol possible, but also for col=0 and r=0 we fix value 0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873308022,"data":"       |                 if col == 0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873309163,"data":"       |                     # must be 0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873310322,"data":"       |                     if 0 in used:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873311468,"data":"       |                         return\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873312605,"data":"       |                     candidates = [0]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.87331375,"data":"       |                 else:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873316283,"data":"       |                     # any unused symbol\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873317529,"data":"       |                     candidates = [v for v in range(n) if v not in used]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873318791,"data":"       |             else:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873319905,"data":"       |                 prev = col_vals[r-1]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873321066,"data":"       |                 # allowed values are prev (diff 0) or prev+1 (diff 1) modulo n\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873322311,"data":"       |                 for v in [(prev)%n, (prev+1)%n]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873323501,"data":"       |                     if v not in used:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873324655,"data":"       |                         candidates.append(v)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873325815,"data":"       |                 # remove duplicates\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873327007,"data":"       |                 candidates = list(dict.fromkeys(candidates))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873328205,"data":"       |             # iterate candidates\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873329367,"data":"       |             for v in candidates:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873330505,"data":"       |                 # assign\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.87333162,"data":"       |                 col_vals[r] = v\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873332746,"data":"       |                 row_used[r].add(v)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873333894,"data":"       |                 # Continue to next row\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873335087,"data":"       |                 fill_row(r+1, v)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873336263,"data":"       |                 # backtrack\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873337391,"data":"       |                 row_used[r].remove(v)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.87333854,"data":"       |                 col_vals[r] = None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873339679,"data":"       |         fill_row(0, None)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873340829,"data":"       |     backtrack(0, [])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873341943,"data":"       |     return total\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873343085,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873346419,"data":"       | for n in range(2,6):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3925.873355811,"data":"       |     print(n, count_H_matrices(n))\n"}
