,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.185531964,"data":"       | If t ≤ 0, then condition always satisfied (full square). If t \u003e 2, no points. But t ranges from when a=0: t = 7/4 = 1.75. When a=1: t = (7 - 2)/4 = 5/4 = 1.25. So t is between 1.25 and 1.75, always between 0 and 2. So region is a subset of square where b + c ≥ t.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.185533513,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.185534897,"data":"       | Thus for each a, area in (b,c) plane = area of region in unit square where b + c ≥ t.\n"}
