,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.185761254,"data":"       | analysisWe need to parse the problem: Cube-shaped container (a cube). Vertices A,B,C,D are such that AB and CD are parallel edges of the cube, and AC and BD are diagonals of faces of the cube. So they form a rectangle ABDC? Wait rectangle ABDC? The rectangle ABDC is formed by vertices A,B,D,C? Let's think.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.185764574,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.18576573,"data":"       | In a cube, there are many vertices. Typically, a cube has 8 vertices. The problem selects four vertices A,B,C,D such that AB and CD are parallel edges, and AC and BD are face diagonals. This configuration corresponds to a \"skew rectangle\" across the cube: A and B are adjacent vertices (edge AB). C and D are opposite vertices? Let's draw.\n"}
