,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.185768458,"data":"       | Consider a cube with coordinates: Let's set the cube side length s (unknown). Choose coordinate system: Let the cube be oriented arbitrarily in space. But we have constraints about heights above plane P (horizontal plane). The plane of rectangle ABDC is perpendicular to P. So rectangle ABDC is a plane that is vertical (perpendicular to horizontal plane). So rectangle ABDC is a vertical rectangle within the cube.\n"}
