,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.187193365,"data":"       | Thus for (y,z) with y+z ≤ 7.5, x can go up to 6 (full range). For y+z \u003e 7.5, x max is 21 - 2y - 2z (\u003c6). Also need positivity: 21 - 2y - 2z \u003e 0 → y+z \u003c 10.5. So region where y+z between 7.5 and 10.5 gives truncated x.\n"}
