,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189026658,"data":"       | Cross product formula: For vectors a = (a_x, a_y, a_z), b = (b_x, b_y, b_z), a × b = (a_y b_z - a_z b_y, a_z b_x - a_x b_z, a_x b_y - a_y b_x). So n_z = a_x b_y - a_y b_x = u_x (v_y + w_y) - u_y (v_x + w_x).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189028184,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189029313,"data":"       | Thus condition n_z = 0 =\u003e u_x (v_y + w_y) = u_y (v_x + w_x).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189030576,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189031676,"data":"       | That's one equation.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.18903417,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189035334,"data":"       | Additionally, orthogonality conditions:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189036557,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189037686,"data":"       | u·v = u_x v_x + u_y v_y + u_z v_z = 0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189038947,"data":"       | u·w = u_x w_x + u_y w_y + u_z w_z = 0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189040187,"data":"       | v·w = v_x w_x + v_y w_y + v_z w_z = 0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189041375,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189042516,"data":"       | Lengths: u_x^2 + u_y^2 + u_z^2 = s^2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189043748,"data":"       | v_x^2 + v_y^2 + v_z^2 = s^2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189044921,"data":"       | w_x^2 + w_y^2 + w_z^2 = s^2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189046107,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189047245,"data":"       | We also have known z components: u_z = 2, v_z + w_z = 8. Unknown individually v_z, w_z.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189048576,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189049684,"data":"       | We also have that the cube is positioned such that A is on plane P (z=0). No other constraints.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189051038,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189052151,"data":"       | We need to find s, possibly using orthogonality and length constraints.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189053434,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189054591,"data":"       | We have many unknowns (components). However we can use the fact that vectors are orthogonal and equal length, which imposes relationships.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189055991,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189057111,"data":"       | Let’s denote v_z = a, w_z = b, with a + b = 8.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189058361,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189059518,"data":"       | Let’s denote u = (u_x, u_y, 2). Since |u|^2 = s^2 =\u003e u_x^2 + u_y^2 + 4 = s^2.\n"}
