,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189082082,"data":"       | Thus A, B, C, D form a rectangle that is not a face but a cross-section plane through the cube: rectangle ABDC (maybe order A-B-D-C). Indeed rectangle ABDC is formed by edges AB and CD (parallel) and diagonals AC and BD (cross). This rectangle is a plane cutting through the cube, presumably perpendicular to horizontal plane P.\n"}
