,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189084962,"data":"       | Given: Vertex A is set on horizontal plane P, and the plane of rectangle ABDC is perpendicular to P. So the rectangle ABDC is vertical (perpendicular to ground). B is 2 meters above P, C is 8 m above P, D is 10 m above P. So A is on plane (height 0). So we have heights (z-coordinates) for A=0, B=2, C=8, D=10.\n"}
