,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189090684,"data":"       | We have a cube container with water surface parallel to plane P (i.e., horizontal) at height 7 meters above P. So water fills lower part of cube up to height 7. Since cube may be tilted (its orientation is not axis-aligned with P). We need volume of water inside cube (i.e., portion of cube below plane z=7). The cube side length unknown but can be derived from distances between vertices.\n"}
