,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189151251,"data":"       | We need to determine s (edge length) and geometry to compute volume of portion of cube below z=7.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.18915258,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189153686,"data":"       | The cube is oriented arbitrarily but we have enough constraints to solve for s and orientation.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189156398,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.18915756,"data":"       | Let's set up unknowns and solve.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189158792,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189159937,"data":"       | Let e1 = (p, q, 2). Let e2 = (r, s2, u). Let e3 = (t, v, w). (I'll rename to avoid confusion with side length s). Let's call side length L.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189161369,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189162511,"data":"       | Constraints:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189163649,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189164803,"data":"       | 1) p^2 + q^2 + 4 = L^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189165978,"data":"       | 2) r^2 + s2^2 + u^2 = L^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189167146,"data":"       | 3) t^2 + v^2 + w^2 = L^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189168313,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189169422,"data":"       | Orthogonality:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189170626,"data":"       | 4) p*r + q*s2 + 2*u = 0 (e1·e2 =0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189171855,"data":"       | 5) p*t + q*v + 2*w = 0 (e1·e3 =0)\n"}
