,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189178882,"data":"       | 8) s2 + v = Y (horizontal y component)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189180113,"data":"       | 9) u + w = 8.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189181258,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.189182413,"data":"       | But we don't know X,Y. However we can use that length of AC is L*sqrt(2) (diagonal of face). Indeed AC = e2 + e3, and e2, e3 are orthogonal, same length L, so magnitude sqrt(L^2 + L^2) = L*sqrt(2). So:\n"}
