,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190862334,"data":"       | analysisThe determinant is s^4 * (-p**2 - q**2 + s**2 - 4). Set determinant = 0. Since s\u003e0, s^4 ≠ 0, so we must have:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190863747,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190864876,"data":"       | -s^2? Wait expression: -p**2 - q**2 + s**2 - 4 = 0 =\u003e s^2 = p^2 + q^2 + 4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190866222,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190867314,"data":"       | Thus we have relationship:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190868491,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190869583,"data":"       | s^2 = p^2 + q^2 + 4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190870724,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19087192,"data":"       | Interesting! This ties s to p,q.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190873081,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190874242,"data":"       | We also have earlier inequality s^2 ≥ p^2 + q^2 (derived from Cauchy). This now says s^2 = p^2 + q^2 + 4, which is stronger.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190877527,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190878676,"data":"       | Thus we have:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19087983,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190880936,"data":"       | s^2 = p^2 + q^2 + 4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190882082,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190883234,"data":"       | Now also we have p+q = 8.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19088444,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190885543,"data":"       | Thus we can solve for p,q and s.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190886729,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190887834,"data":"       | Let’s solve:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190889019,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19089016,"data":"       | Let’s set p+q=8. Let’s denote sum = 8, sum of squares = p^2 + q^2 = (p+q)^2 - 2pq = 64 - 2pq.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190891511,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190892654,"data":"       | Thus s^2 = (64 - 2pq) + 4 = 68 - 2pq.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190893843,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190894947,"data":"       | Thus s^2 = 68 - 2pq.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190896124,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190897251,"data":"       | Also we have s^2 must be \u003e= (p+q)^2? Not necessarily. But we have s^2 \u003e= p^2 + q^2 + 4 ( equality). So okay.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190898659,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190899775,"data":"       | Now we also have p,q positive, each ≤ s (since each component cannot exceed length). Let's compute possible values.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190901126,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19090226,"data":"       | We need also that s^2 = p^2 + q^2 + 4, and s^2 = u_h^2 + 4, but not needed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190903518,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190904633,"data":"       | From s^2 = 68 - 2pq, we can express pq in terms of s^2:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190905887,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190906978,"data":"       | pq = (68 - s^2)/2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190908132,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190909236,"data":"       | But also we have relation between p,q from sum and product: given sum =8, product = pq.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190910528,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190911656,"data":"       | Thus p and q are roots of quadratic t^2 - 8 t + pq = 0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190912889,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190914382,"data":"       | Thus discriminant Δ = 64 - 4 pq = 64 - 4 * ((68 - s^2)/2) = 64 - 2*(68 - s^2) = 64 - 136 + 2 s^2 = 2 s^2 - 72.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190916725,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19091854,"data":"       | Thus discriminant must be non-negative: 2 s^2 - 72 ≥ 0 =\u003e s^2 ≥ 36 =\u003e s ≥ 6, consistent earlier.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.190920856,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19092279,"data":"       | Thus p,q = (8 ± sqrt(2 s^2 - 72))/2 = 4 ± sqrt( (2 s^2 - 72) )/2? Wait compute:\n"}
