,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19106638,"data":"       | But we might need to consider only water inside cube, regardless of whether part of cube is below ground. So we can allow v_z or w_z negative. However v_z = p and w_z = q represent vertical components of edges from A. Since A is at ground, the vertex A+v (call it V) would have height p. If p negative, that vertex would be below ground. That's possible.\n"}
