,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191701132,"data":"       | analysisLet's compute V0 via direct formula:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191703478,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191704638,"data":"       | V0 = area(R1) + (1/2) * ∫_{R2} (7 - p b - q c) db dc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191705957,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191707087,"data":"       | But ∫_{R2} (7 - p b - q c) = ∫_{region where 5 \u003c p b + q c ≤ 7} (7 - p b - q c) db dc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191708512,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191709689,"data":"       | We can compute this integral by evaluating total integral over region where p b + q c ≤ 7 minus integral over region where p b + q c ≤ 5.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191711153,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191712327,"data":"       | Let’s define S(K) = ∫_{p b + q c ≤ K} (7 - p b - q c) db dc over unit square. But note that integrand depends on K? Actually we can compute I(K) = ∫_{p b + q c ≤ K} (p b + q c) db dc (the integral of linear function). Then ∫_{region ≤K} (7 - p b - q c) = 7 * A(K) - I(K). So we need I(K) for K=7 and K=5.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191714182,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191715294,"data":"       | Thus we need area A(K) (computed) and integral of p b + q c over region.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191716581,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191717731,"data":"       | Compute J(K) = ∫_{region ≤K} (p b + q c) db dc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191719164,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191720324,"data":"       | We can compute J(K) using integration similarly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191721551,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191722676,"data":"       | Given region defined by inequality, we can integrate: ∫_{b=0}^{b_max} ∫_{c=0}^{c_max(b)} (p b + q c) dc db.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191724073,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191725187,"data":"       | Where c_max(b) = min( (K - p b)/q, 1) for b where K - p b ≥ 0 else 0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191726485,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191727611,"data":"       | We can compute J(K) piecewise similar to area.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191728803,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191729911,"data":"       | Let's compute symbolic formulas for J(K) using sympy piecewise integration as we did for area.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191731219,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191732334,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codedef J_K(K):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19173384,"data":"       |     b = sp.symbols('b', real=True)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191735042,"data":"       |     # define b_star and b0 as before\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191736227,"data":"       |     b_star = (K - q)/p\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191737384,"data":"       |     b0 = K/p\n"}
