,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191828802,"data":"       | analysisThus J(K) piecewise.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191830014,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191831234,"data":"       | Now we compute V0 = A5 + (1/2)*(7*A7 - J7 - (7*A5 - J5))? Wait we need integral over region R2 of (7 - p b - q c)/2. R2 = region where 5 \u003c p b + q c ≤ 7.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191834184,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191835409,"data":"       | Thus ∫_{R2} (7 - p b - q c) db dc = ∫_{≤7} (7 - ...) - ∫_{≤5} (7 - ...) = (7 A7 - J7) - (7 A5 - J5) = 7 (A7 - A5) - (J7 - J5).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191836893,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191838006,"data":"       | Thus water volume fraction:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191839212,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191840338,"data":"       | V0 = A5 + (1/2) * [ 7 (A7 - A5) - (J7 - J5) ].\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191841577,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191842682,"data":"       | Simplify.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191843806,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19184496,"data":"       | Let's compute symbolic piecewise for p≥? Need to consider p relative to 5 and 7.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191846273,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191847362,"data":"       | We have three regimes:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19184858,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191849919,"data":"       | 1) p ≥ 7 (implies p ≥ 5 automatically). Then both area formulas use first piece for both K=5 and K=7. So we can compute V0 with those formulas.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191851428,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191852571,"data":"       | 2) 5 ≤ p \u003c 7. Then for K=5 we use first piece (p≥5), for K=7 we use second piece (p\u003cK). So mixed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191854038,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191855159,"data":"       | 3) p \u003c 5 (i.e., p between 0 and 5). Then both use second piece.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191856438,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191857551,"data":"       | But recall p≥q, and q=8-p, so p≥4. So p ∈ [4,8]. So p\u003c5 region is p∈[4,5). So we need to handle that.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191858982,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191860088,"data":"       | Thus we have three intervals: [4,5), [5,7), [7,8].\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191861331,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191862422,"data":"       | Let's compute V0 expressions for each interval using sympy.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191863678,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19186476,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codep=sp.symbols('p', real=True)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191865982,"data":"       | q=8-p\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191867094,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191868248,"data":"       | # define A5, A7, J5, J7 using piecewise definitions from earlier functions\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191869522,"data":"       | def A_K(K):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191870664,"data":"       |     b_star = (K - q)/p\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19187181,"data":"       |     b0 = K/p\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19187297,"data":"       |     # piecewise as before\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191874404,"data":"       |     expr1 = b_star + (1/q)*(K*(b0 - b_star) - p/2*(b0**2 - b_star**2))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191875679,"data":"       |     expr2 = b_star + (1/q)*(K*(1 - b_star) - p/2*(1 - b_star**2))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.191878867,"data":"       |     return sp.Piecewise((sp.simplify(expr1), sp.Ge(p, K)), (sp.simplify(expr2), True))\n"}
