,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.192298106,"data":"       | Let’s define inequality: 2a + 4b + 4c ≤ 7.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.192299378,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.192300476,"data":"       | We can solve for a: a ≤ (7 - 4b - 4c)/2 = 3.5 - 2b - 2c.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.192301751,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.192302923,"data":"       | But a ∈ [0,1]; so a_max = min(1, 3.5 - 2b - 2c). Since 3.5 - 2b - 2c is at most 3.5 (when b=c=0), which is \u003e1, so for some region a_max=1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.192304394,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.192305512,"data":"       | Find region where 3.5 - 2b - 2c ≥ 1 =\u003e 2b + 2c ≤ 2.5 =\u003e b + c ≤ 1.25.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.192306952,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.192308044,"data":"       | Since b,c ∈ [0,1], this region is the set of points where b + c ≤ 1.25.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.192309379,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.192310475,"data":"       | Thus region where a_max=1 corresponds to b + c ≤ 1.25.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.192311758,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.192312955,"data":"       | Otherwise, where 1.25 \u003c b + c ≤ something else (max value where a_max \u003e=0). The inequality a_max≥0 requires 3.5 - 2b - 2c ≥ 0 =\u003e b + c ≤ 1.75.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.192314536,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.192315698,"data":"       | Thus for b + c between 1.25 and 1.75, a_max = 3.5 - 2b - 2c (which lies between 0 and 1). For b + c \u003e 1.75, no a allowed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19231708,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19231822,"data":"       | Thus we can compute volume:\n"}
