his rectangle is a rectangle with side lengths equal to side length s (AB) and s*sqrt(2) (BD). So rectangle's dimensions: width = s (distance AB), height = s*sqrt(2) (distance between AB and CD along diagonal direction). The plane of rectangle is perpendicular to ground plane P. So rectangle stands vertically.\n"}
