,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.194191051,"data":"       | We can w.l.o.g. assume a \u003c= b (i.e., a \u003c=4). Because if a \u003e4, then b \u003c4, so b is smaller. So we can treat case with smaller a ≤4? Actually a could be up to 8, but the smaller of the two is at most 4 (by sum 8). So the smaller side length a_min ≤4. So we can designate a = min(pz,qz) ≤4, b = max(pz,qz) = 8 - a ≥4.\n"}
