,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.194206699,"data":"       | - If b ≤5 (i.e., 4 ≤ b ≤5). Since a = 8 - b, then a ≥3. So both a,b ≤5? Actually if b ≤5, then a = 8 - b ≥3. So both ≤5 (since a could be up to 5). Then for all T ∈ [5,7], we have T \u003e= b? Actually T max 7 \u003e b; T min 5 could be equal to b if b=5, else greater if b\u003c5. So T \u003e= b for all α. So T is greater than both a,b.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.194208766,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.194210105,"data":"       | Thus for all T, we are in case where T \u003e max(a,b) (i.e., both intercepts \u003e1). So area formula is: area = 1 - 1/2 * (1 - (T-a)/b) * (1 - (T-b)/a). However need to ensure (T-a)/b ≤1 and (T-b)/a ≤1; these hold because T ≤ a+b=8, and if T \u003e= max(a,b), the derived intersections will be within [0,1].\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.194213127,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.194214286,"data":"       | - If b \u003e5 (i.e., 5 \u003c b ≤8). Then a = 8 - b \u003c3. So a \u003c3 (\u003c5). In this case, for T in [5,7], we have T \u003e a (always) but T may be less than b for some α: Since T max 7, if b \u003e7, then T \u003c b for all α. If b between 5 and7, then T may be greater than b for some T (like T=7 \u003e b maybe if b\u003c7) but T=5 may be less than b. So we have region where T can be either less than b or greater than b.\n"}
