,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.194220078,"data":"       | Specifically, define α0 where T = 7 - 2α = b =\u003e α = (7 - b)/2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.194221471,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19422259,"data":"       | If b between 5 and7, then α0 in [0,1]. For α less than α0 (i.e., T \u003e b), we are in case T \u003e b (both intercepts \u003e1). For α greater than α0 (i.e., T \u003c b), we are in case a \u003c T \u003c b (since T still \u003e a). That's the intermediate case where one intercept \u003e1 and the other \u003c=1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.194224575,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.194225662,"data":"       | If b \u003e=7, then α0 \u003c=0? Actually if b \u003e=7, then T never exceeds b for α in [0,1] (since max T =7 \u003c= b), so we are always in case a \u003c T \u003c= b.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.194227282,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4140.19422841,"data":"       | Thus there are three regimes:\n"}
