,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437240147,"data":"       | The determinant of this matrix is known: For matrix with a on diagonal, b off-diagonal (symmetric), determinant = (a - b)^2 (a + 2b). Let's verify: For 3x3 matrix with diagonal a and off-diagonal b, eigenvalues: λ1 = a + 2b (vector (1,1,1)), λ2 = a - b (multiplicity 2) (vectors orthogonal to (1,1,1)). So determinant = (a+2b)*(a-b)^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437241849,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437242932,"data":"       | Thus V^2 = det(G) = (13 - d)^2 * (13 + 2d). Wait careful: a = 13, b = d. So determinant = (13 - d)^2 * (13 + 2d). Good.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437244318,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437245384,"data":"       | Thus V = sqrt(det(G)). Since V positive.\n"}
