,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43730014,"data":"       | Now confirm that there are exactly two noncongruent parallelepipeds: one acute (d positive) and one obtuse (d negative). The ratio of volumes is 63/62.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43730147,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437302483,"data":"       | Thus answer m+n = 125.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437303565,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437304616,"data":"       | Let's double-check using random vectors that satisfy constraints.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437305795,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437306913,"data":"       | We can construct vectors a,b,c with given dot products. For d positive: choose a = (sqrt(13),0,0). Choose b such that dot product = d and length sqrt(13). Solve for b = (x,y,0). Then x = d/|a| = d/ sqrt(13). Since a·b = sqrt(13)*x = d =\u003e x = d/ sqrt(13). Then length condition: x^2 + y^2 = 13 =\u003e y = sqrt(13 - x^2). Similarly choose c with same dot product with a and b. Could solve but not needed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437308804,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437309855,"data":"       | Compute volume using cross product to verify numeric.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437311008,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437312162,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codeimport math, random\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437313489,"data":"       | s=math.sqrt(13)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437314544,"data":"       | d=5/2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437315635,"data":"       | # define a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437316702,"data":"       | a = (s,0,0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43731774,"data":"       | # define b\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437318807,"data":"       | x = d/s\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437319912,"data":"       | y = math.sqrt(13 - x**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437321022,"data":"       | b = (x, y, 0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437322156,"data":"       | # define c such that dot with a = d, dot with b = d, length sqrt(13)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437323375,"data":"       | # Let c = (x, u, v). Dot with a: s*x = d =\u003e x = d/s (same as b)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437324575,"data":"       | x = d/s\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437326197,"data":"       | # unknown u,v such that dot with b: x*x + y*u = d =\u003e x**2 + y*u = d =\u003e u = (d - x**2)/y\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437327484,"data":"       | u = (d - x**2)/y\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437328599,"data":"       | # length condition: x**2 + u**2 + v**2 = 13 =\u003e v = sqrt(13 - x**2 - u**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437329875,"data":"       | v = math.sqrt(13 - x**2 - u**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437330939,"data":"       | c = (x, u, v)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437332018,"data":"       | def dot(p,q):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437333099,"data":"       |     return sum(p[i]*q[i] for i in range(3))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437336255,"data":"       | def cross(p,q):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437337375,"data":"       |     return (p[1]*q[2]-p[2]*q[1], p[2]*q[0]-p[0]*q[2], p[0]*q[1]-p[1]*q[0])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437338603,"data":"       | def triple(p,q,r):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437339664,"data":"       |     cr = cross(q,r)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437340744,"data":"       |     return dot(p,cr)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437341859,"data":"       | vol = abs(triple(a,b,c))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437342975,"data":"       | vol, (63/math.sqrt(2))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437344069,"data":"       | \n"}
