,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437445734,"data":"       \u003e 43.840620433565945 43.84062043356595\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43744687,"data":"       \u003e \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437447951,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437449056,"data":"     [Turn 4]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437450094,"data":"     [Reasoning] (2394 chars):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43745114,"data":"       | analysisMatches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437453892,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43745508,"data":"       | Thus ratio = (63/2)/31 = 63/62.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437456182,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437457199,"data":"       | Thus answer 125.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437458281,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437459474,"data":"       | Now produce final answer.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437460559,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437461645,"data":"       | assistantfinalFor a parallelepiped let the three edge vectors be \\(\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b},\\mathbf{c}\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437463182,"data":"       | Each face is a rhombus whose sides are the two edge vectors spanning that face.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437464405,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43746539,"data":"       | ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437466437,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437467467,"data":"       | ### 1.  Length of the edges  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437468527,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437469566,"data":"       | For a rhombus with diagonals \\(p,q\\) and side length \\(s\\),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43747089,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.4374719,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437472994,"data":"       | p^{2}+q^{2}=4s^{2}\\qquad\\text{(parallelogram law)}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437474265,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437475295,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437476345,"data":"       | Here \\(p=\\sqrt{21},\\;q=\\sqrt{31}\\); thus  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43747762,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437478639,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43747972,"data":"       | 4s^{2}=21+31=52\\Longrightarrow s^{2}=13\\Longrightarrow s=\\sqrt{13}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437481017,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437482032,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437483073,"data":"       | Hence \\(|\\mathbf a|=|\\mathbf b|=|\\mathbf c|=\\sqrt{13}\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437484348,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437485372,"data":"       | ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437486404,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437487435,"data":"       | ### 2.  Dot product of any two edges  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437488543,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437489615,"data":"       | For two equal‑length vectors \\(\\mathbf u,\\mathbf v\\) (\\(|\\mathbf u|=|\\mathbf v|=s\\)),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437491097,"data":"       | the diagonals of the rhombus they span are \\(\\mathbf u+\\mathbf v\\) and \\(\\mathbf u-\\mathbf v\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437492528,"data":"       | Their squared lengths are  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437493609,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43749463,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437495675,"data":"       | |\\mathbf u+\\mathbf v|^{2}=2s^{2}+2\\mathbf u\\!\\cdot\\!\\mathbf v,\\qquad\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437497044,"data":"       | |\\mathbf u-\\mathbf v|^{2}=2s^{2}-2\\mathbf u\\!\\cdot\\!\\mathbf v .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437499855,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437500919,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437501957,"data":"       | These must be \\(21\\) and \\(31\\).  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437503227,"data":"       | Since \\(2s^{2}=2\\cdot13=26\\),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437504582,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437505642,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437506699,"data":"       | 26\\pm2\\mathbf u\\!\\cdot\\!\\mathbf v = 21,\\;31\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437507935,"data":"       | \\Longrightarrow \\mathbf u\\!\\cdot\\!\\mathbf v =\\pm\\frac52 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437509456,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437510495,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437511527,"data":"       | Thus for any pair of edges  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437512615,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437513613,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437514826,"data":"       | \\mathbf a\\!\\cdot\\!\\mathbf b=\\mathbf a\\!\\cdot\\!\\mathbf c=\\mathbf b\\!\\cdot\\!\\mathbf c = d,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437516195,"data":"       | \\qquad d=\\pm\\frac52 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43751727,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437518305,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437519322,"data":"       | The sign gives two different shapes: an acute‑angled rhombohedron (\\(d=+\\frac52\\))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437520748,"data":"       | and an obtuse‑angled one (\\(d=-\\frac52\\)). They are not congruent because the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437522059,"data":"       | angle between edges is invariant under isometries.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437523144,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437524199,"data":"       | ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437525216,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437526247,"data":"       | ### 3.  Volume from the Gram determinant  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437527317,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437528352,"data":"       | The volume \\(V\\) satisfies  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.4375295,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43753049,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43753151,"data":"       | V^{2}= \\det G,\\qquad \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437532649,"data":"       | G=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437533756,"data":"       | 13 \u0026 d \u0026 d\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437534992,"data":"       | d \u0026 13 \u0026 d\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437536193,"data":"       | d \u0026 d \u0026 13\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437537328,"data":"       | \\end{pmatrix}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437538413,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437539424,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437540465,"data":"       | For a matrix with diagonal \\(a\\) and off‑diagonal \\(b\\),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437541764,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437542777,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43754388,"data":"       | \\det = (a-b)^{2}(a+2b).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437546883,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437547953,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437549001,"data":"       | Here \\(a=13,\\;b=d\\), so  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437550145,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437551146,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437552215,"data":"       | V^{2}= (13-d)^{2}\\,(13+2d).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437553329,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437554345,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437555352,"data":"       | * For \\(d=+\\frac52\\):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437556482,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437557507,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437558569,"data":"       | V_{+}^{2}= (13-\\tfrac52)^{2}\\,(13+5)=\\frac{3969}{2}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437559865,"data":"       | \\Longrightarrow V_{+}= \\frac{63}{\\sqrt2}= \\frac{63\\sqrt2}{2}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437561166,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437562246,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437563261,"data":"       | * For \\(d=-\\frac52\\):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437564401,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437565399,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437566468,"data":"       | V_{-}^{2}= (13+\\tfrac52)^{2}\\,(13-5)=1922=2\\cdot31^{2}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437567757,"data":"       | \\Longrightarrow V_{-}=31\\sqrt2 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437568885,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437569934,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437570985,"data":"       | Hence \\(V_{+}\u003eV_{-}\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43757217,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437573161,"data":"       | ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437574187,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437575205,"data":"       | ### 4.  Ratio of the volumes  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437576271,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43757728,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.43757834,"data":"       | \\frac{V_{+}}{V_{-}}=\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437579422,"data":"       | \\frac{\\dfrac{63\\sqrt2}{2}}{31\\sqrt2}= \\frac{63}{62}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437580699,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.437581714,"data":"       | \n"}
