,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4194.439039454,"data":"       | Let’s set up unknowns: Let |a| = |b| = p (since a and b sides of rhombus). Similarly, |a| = |c| = p' maybe not same? Wait condition says each face is a rhombus, but not necessarily that all edges have same length. The rhombus condition for face spanned by a and b: requires |a| = |b| (edges of that face). However a also is edge of face with c, requiring |a| = |c|. Similarly, b with c require |b| = |c|. So all three edges have equal length: |a| = |b| = |c| = L. Because each pair must have equal side lengths. So all three vectors have same magnitude L.\n"}
