,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.936797115,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.936798156,"data":"       | But maybe s and t are roots of x^4 - √17 x^2 + 4 = 0? Let's compute: Since s^2 + t^2 = √17, s^2 t^2 = 4. So s^2 and t^2 are roots of quadratic u^2 - √17 u + 4 = 0. Indeed u^2 - (s^2 + t^2) u + s^2 t^2 = 0. So u = s^2, t^2 satisfy u^2 - √17 u + 4 = 0. So s^2, t^2 are algebraic degree 2 over Q(√17). But we can treat them.\n"}
