,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.93709784,"data":"       | We have b_1 = 9 mod10 = 9. b_2 = 49 mod10 = 9. Recurrence: b_k ≡ 9 b_{k-1} - 16 b_{k-2} (mod 10). Since modulo 10, -16 ≡ -6 ≡ 4 (since -16 mod10 = 4). Actually -16 ≡ (10-6)=4. So recurrence mod10: b_k ≡ 9 b_{k-1} + 4 b_{k-2} (mod 10). Because -16 ≡ 4.\n"}
