,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.9385061,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.938507159,"data":"       | Also product: s^2 * t^2 = ((√17 + 1)/2) * ((√17 - 1)/2) = ( ( (√17)^2 - 1^2 ) ) /4 = (17 - 1)/4 = 16/4 = 4. So s^2 * t^2 = 4 =\u003e (s t)^2 = 4 =\u003e s t = 2 (positive). Indeed sec * tan = (1/cos)*(sin/cos) = sin/(cos^2) =? Let's check: sec * tan = (1/cos)*(sin/cos) = sin / cos^2. Using sin = 2 cos^2, gives sin / cos^2 = 2. So indeed s t = 2. Good.\n"}
