,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.939913118,"data":"       | Observation: s and t are positive real numbers, both \u003e0. They satisfy s^2 - t^2 = 1, and also s t =? Let's compute product: s * t = sqrt( ((1+√17)/2) * ((-1+√17)/2) ) = sqrt( ( ( (√17)^2 - 1 ) ) /4 ) = sqrt( ( 17 - 1 ) /4 ) = sqrt(16/4) = sqrt(4) = 2. So s t = 2. Indeed because s^2 * t^2 = ((1+√17)(-1+√17))/4 = ( ( (√17)^2 - 1) )/4 = (17 - 1)/4 = 16/4 = 4, so s t = 2 (positive). Good.\n"}
