,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.940769532,"data":"       | c_n = s^{2n} + t^{2n}. For n=1 (i.e., exponent 2): sqrt(17) (non-integer). n=2 (exponent 4): 9 integer. n=3 (exponent 6): 5 sqrt(17). n=4 (exponent 8): 49 integer. So pattern: c_n integer if n even, else sqrt(17) times integer. So indeed c_{2m} = s^{4m} + t^{4m} integer.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.940771021,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.940772039,"data":"       | Thus we can define a_m = c_{2m} = s^{4m} + t^{4m}.\n"}
