,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941236138,"data":"       | Thus s and s' are algebraic conjugates? Not exactly; they are swapped under transformation sqrt(17) -\u003e sqrt(17) (i.e., same sign). But they are not Galois conjugates (the other root would have minus sign). However they are related via product 4.\n"}
