,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941933919,"data":"       | Given acute angle A with tan A = 2 cos A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941935075,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941936196,"data":"       | We need to find number of positive integers n ≤ 1000 such that sec^n A + tan^n A is a positive integer whose units digit (i.e., last digit) is 9.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941939036,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941940156,"data":"       | We must compute value of sec A and tan A (they are positive since acute). Then expression E_n = sec^n A + tan^n A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941941446,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941942556,"data":"       | We must see for which n (positive integer ≤1000) this quantity is integer and ends with digit 9.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941943879,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941944975,"data":"       | We need to find A satisfying tan A = 2 cos A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941946139,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941947259,"data":"       | Let's solve equation: tan A = 2 cos A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941948422,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941949489,"data":"       | tan A = sin A / cos A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941950629,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941951729,"data":"       | Thus sin A / cos A = 2 cos A → sin A = 2 cos^2 A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941952942,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941954032,"data":"       | Since cos^2 A = (1+cos 2A)/2? But maybe solve.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941955198,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941956281,"data":"       | Let cos A = c, sin A = s. Then s = 2 c^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941957456,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941958552,"data":"       | But we also have s^2 + c^2 = 1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941959702,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941960788,"data":"       | Thus (2 c^2)^2 + c^2 = 1 → 4 c^4 + c^2 - 1 = 0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941962015,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941963095,"data":"       | Let x = c^2. Then 4 x^2 + x - 1 = 0.\n"}
