,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941983226,"data":"       | Tan A = sin/cos = (2c^2)/c = 2c = 2 sqrt(x). Indeed given tan = 2 cos? Wait we have tan = 2 cos? Actually given tan = 2 cos, not 2c? Wait we derived earlier: tan A = sin / cos = (2c^2) / c = 2c. Yes tan = 2c, but equation says tan = 2 cos, i.e., tan = 2c. So consistent.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941984831,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4266.941985928,"data":"       | Thus tan A = 2 sqrt(x). And sec A = sqrt(1/x).\n"}
