,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4322.289764136,"data":"       | E = C + (30/55)*(A-C) = C*(1 - 30/55) + A*(30/55). Actually A= (0,0). So E = (1 - 30/55) * C = (25/55) * C = (5/11) * C. Because moving from C towards A by proportion 30/55, leaving fraction 25/55 from C to A? Wait: Starting at C, moving towards A by fraction t = 30/55 of the total length. So the new point is C + t*(A-C) = (1 - t) C + t A = (1 - t) C. Since A is zero, yes. So E = (1 - 30/55) C = (25/55) C = (5/11) C. So coordinates: E = (5/11 * 27.5, 5/11 * 55*sqrt(3)/2) = ( (5*27.5)/11, (5*55*sqrt(3)/2)/11 ). Compute: 27.5 = 55/2. So (5*(55/2))/11 = (5*55)/(22) = (275)/22 = 12.5? Let's compute: 275/22 = 12.5 exactly (since 22*12.5=275). Good. So x-coordinate of E = 12.5.\n"}
