,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4322.290395071,"data":"       | analysisWe need to solve geometry problem: equilateral triangle side 55. Points D on BC with BD=7, so BC side length 55, B to C direction. Let BC segment: B at (0,0), C at (55,0) maybe. Then D is on BC with BD=7, so D at (7,0) from B. Similarly, E on CA with CE=30. Wait CA side from C to A. Let's set coordinates: equilateral triangle with side s=55. Choose coordinates: Let B = (0,0), C = (55,0). Then A is at (55/2, (55*sqrt(3))/2) because equilateral triangle height = s*sqrt(3)/2. So A = (27.5, 55*sqrt(3)/2). Compute: 55*sqrt(3)/2 = 27.5*sqrt(3). So A = (27.5, 27.5*sqrt(3)). Good.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4322.290397195,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4322.290398256,"data":"       | Now define points:\n"}
