,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4322.290402594,"data":"       | - E on CA: CE = 30. CA is from C (55,0) to A (27.5, 27.5*sqrt(3)). The length CA = 55. Parameter along CA from C towards A: distance from C to E is CE = 30. So E = C + (30/55)*(A - C). Compute vector A - C = (27.5-55, 27.5*sqrt(3)-0) = (-27.5, 27.5*sqrt(3)). Multiply by 30/55 = 6/11. So E = (55,0) + (6/11)*(-27.5, 27.5*sqrt(3)). Compute -27.5*6/11 = -27.5*6/11 = -(27.5*6)/11 = -(165)/11 = -15. So x-coordinate: 55 - 15 = 40. Good. y-coordinate: 27.5*sqrt(3) * 6/11 = (27.5*6/11)*sqrt(3) = (165/11)*sqrt(3) = 15*sqrt(3). So E = (40, 15*sqrt(3)). Nice.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4322.290404652,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4322.290407888,"data":"       | - F on AB: AF = 40. AB from A (27.5, 27.5*sqrt(3)) to B (0,0). Distance from A to F along AB is AF = 40, but AB length is 55. So F is on AB such that distance from A towards B is 40. Parameter t = 40/55 = 8/11 from A towards B. So F = A + ( - (8/11)*(A - B) )? Actually vector from A to B = B - A = (-27.5, -27.5*sqrt(3)). Multiply by 40/55 = 8/11. So F = A + (8/11)*(B - A) = A + (8/11)*(-27.5, -27.5*sqrt(3)) = (27.5 - (8/11)*27.5, 27.5*sqrt(3) - (8/11)*27.5*sqrt(3)). Compute 27.5*(1 - 8/11) = 27.5*(3/11) = (27.5*3)/11 = 82.5/11 = 7.5. So x = 7.5. y = 27.5*sqrt(3)*(1 - 8/11) = 27.5*sqrt(3)*3/11 = (27.5*3/11)*sqrt(3) = 82.5/11*sqrt(3) = 7.5*sqrt(3). So F = (7.5, 7.5*sqrt(3)). Nice.\n"}
