,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4322.290466523,"data":"       | Thus in triangle AEP, we know side AE length? AE is part of side CA: CA length 55, with CE = 30, so AE = CA - CE = 55 - 30 = 25. Indeed A to E distance is 25 (since CA = 55). So AE = 25.\n"}
