,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4322.290513367,"data":"       | Thus we can think of lines through P that intersect sides at points D,E,F such that each line makes same angle with its respective side. That is, line PD makes angle θ with side BC; line PE makes angle θ with side CA; line PF makes angle θ with side AB. So P is the center of a spiral similarity that sends side BC to side CA to side AB? Wait.\n"}
