,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4322.292265095,"data":"       | E: C + (30/55)*(A-C) = C - (30/55)*(C) because A=0. C = (55/2, 55*sqrt3/2). Multiply by 30/55 = 6/11. So subtract (6/11)*C = ( (6/11)*(55/2) = (330/22)=15? Wait compute: 55/2 * 6/11 = (55*6)/(22) = 330/22 = 15. So x coordinate: 55/2 - 15 = (55 -30)/2 = 25/2 = 12.5. y coordinate: 55*sqrt3/2 *6/11 = (55*6 sqrt3)/(22) = (330 sqrt3)/22 = 15 sqrt3? Wait compute: 55*sqrt3/2 * 6/11 = (55*6 sqrt3)/(22) = (330 sqrt3)/22 = 15 sqrt3. Actually 330/22 = 15. So y coordinate: 55*sqrt3/2 - 15 sqrt3 = (55/2 - 30) sqrt3 = (55 - 60)/2 sqrt3 = -5/2 sqrt3? Wait we need to compute precisely: C.y = 55*sqrt3/2 ≈ 47.6. Subtract 15 sqrt3 ≈ 25.98. So result ≈ 21.6. But earlier we got 25*sqrt3/2 = 12.5*sqrt3 ≈ 21.65. Indeed the coordinate we computed is (25/2, 25*sqrt3/2). Let's verify: 25*sqrt3/2 = (25/2) sqrt3 ≈ 12.5*1.732=21.65. So matches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4322.29226947,"data":"       | \n"}
