,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4322.293226071,"data":"       | We can also provide analytic solution: maybe using law of sines in triangles AEP, BFP, CDP, using Ceva? Another approach: Use trigonometric Ceva: For point P inside triangle, lines through P intersect sides at points D,E,F? Actually D,E,F are given points, not intersection of lines from P to vertices. However we have angles at those points equal: ∠AEP = θ, etc.\n"}
