,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462718801,"data":"       | Interpretation: Q is on AM interior (between A and M). Condition: ∠PBQ = ∠PCQ. These are angles at B and C respectively? Wait: angle PBQ is angle formed by points P-B-Q, i.e., vertex at B, lines BP and BQ. Similarly PCQ is angle at C, lines CP and CQ. So we need Q such that the angle between BP and BQ equals angle between CP and CQ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462721498,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462723212,"data":"       | Thus Q is such that BQ and CQ are symmetric with respect to some line? Not exactly.\n"}
