,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462728894,"data":"       | We can treat as condition: The oriented angle between BP and BQ equals oriented angle between CP and CQ. Equivalent to: the rays BQ and CQ are such that the measure of angle between BP and BQ equals measure between CP and CQ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462731323,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462733022,"data":"       | We can perhaps use law of sines in triangles PBQ and PCQ? Not directly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.4627349,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462736603,"data":"       | Better approach: Use complex numbers or vectors.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462738383,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462740105,"data":"       | Let’s denote coordinates of Q = point on AM: Q = A + s*(M-A) where s ∈ (0,1). Equivalent to parameter t earlier: t = s (since we used t from A to M). So Q = (5+2s, 12-12s) with 0 \u003c s \u003c 1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462742462,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462744414,"data":"       | We need angle PBQ = PCQ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462746277,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462747954,"data":"       | Angle between vectors BP and BQ equals angle between CP and CQ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462749801,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462751524,"data":"       | Let’s compute using dot product: cos of angle between vectors u and v is (u·v)/(|u||v|). So condition cos(PBQ) = cos(PCQ). However equality of angles (0 to π) may also be satisfied by supplementary angles (i.e., cos equal but angle may be same or supplementary). But given geometry likely acute? Let's examine.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462754213,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462755928,"data":"       | Angles PBQ and PCQ are likely both acute? Not sure. We'll enforce equality of the angle measure (0 to π). Since both are between lines from B and C to P and Q, they likely are acute.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46275822,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462759907,"data":"       | Thus we can set:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462761652,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462763334,"data":"       | cos ∠PBQ = ( (P-B)·(Q-B) ) / (|P-B||Q-B| )\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462765257,"data":"       | cos ∠PCQ = ( (P-C)·(Q-C) ) / (|P-C||Q-C| )\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462767088,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462768749,"data":"       | Set them equal.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462770513,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46277215,"data":"       | Alternatively we could set squared sines equal etc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462773997,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462775715,"data":"       | But we also have Q on line AM; we can solve for s.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462777535,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462779252,"data":"       | Let's compute using sympy rationally.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46278104,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462782687,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codes = sp.symbols('s', real=True)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462784587,"data":"       | Q = sp.Point(5+2*s, 12-12*s)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462786324,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46278807,"data":"       | # vectors\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462792534,"data":"       | BP = P - B\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462794322,"data":"       | BQ = Q - B\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462796043,"data":"       | CP = P - C\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.4627977,"data":"       | CQ = Q - C\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462799401,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462801563,"data":"       | # dot products\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462803343,"data":"       | dot1 = BP.dot(BQ)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462805047,"data":"       | dot2 = CP.dot(CQ)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46280683,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46280844,"data":"       | # squared lengths\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462810152,"data":"       | normBP2 = BP.dot(BP)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462811852,"data":"       | normBQ2 = BQ.dot(BQ)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462813537,"data":"       | normCP2 = CP.dot(CP)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462815267,"data":"       | normCQ2 = CQ.dot(CQ)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.462816982,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46281866,"data":"       | expr = sp.simplify(dot1/sp.sqrt(normBP2*normBQ2) - dot2/sp.sqrt(normCP2*normCQ2))\n"}
