,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.463488264,"data":"       | Let's set up coordinate system: easier to place triangle with known side lengths. Use coordinates: Place B at (0,0), C at (14,0) (since BC=14). Then we need A such that AB=13, AC=15. So coordinates of A = (x_A, y_A) with distances to B and C.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.463490669,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.463492445,"data":"       | From B: x_A^2 + y_A^2 = 13^2 = 169.\n"}
