,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.463899662,"data":"       | We can rewrite as m / √n: Multiply numerator and denominator to rationalize: Suppose we set m/√n = (99√37)/74 =\u003e cross multiply: m = (99√37)/74 * √n =\u003e m = (99√(37 n))/74. For m integer, need n such that 37 n is a perfect square times denominator? Hmm.\n"}
