,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465429032,"data":"       | analysisWe need to solve geometry problem. Triangle with sides 13,14,15. M is midpoint of BC. P is point on circumcircle such that M lies on line AP (i.e., AP passes through M). There exists unique point Q on segment AM such that angle PBQ = angle PCQ. Find AQ length expressed as m/sqrt(n). Compute m+n.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465431558,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465433244,"data":"       | We need to compute length AQ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465435076,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465436782,"data":"       | We have triangle coordinates. Let's set coordinates: convenient to place B at (0,0), C at (14,0) (since BC=14). Then we need coordinates of A such that AB=13, AC=15.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465438913,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465440597,"data":"       | Let B(0,0), C(14,0). Let A = (x_A, y_A) with y\u003e0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465444362,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465446059,"data":"       | AB^2 = x_A^2 + y_A^2 = 13^2 = 169.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465447836,"data":"       | AC^2 = (x_A-14)^2 + y_A^2 = 15^2 = 225.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46544964,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465451326,"data":"       | Subtract: (x_A-14)^2 - x_A^2 = 225-169 = 56.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46545313,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465454836,"data":"       | Compute: (x_A^2 -28x_A +196) - x_A^2 = -28x_A +196 =56 =\u003e -28x_A = -140 =\u003e x_A = 5.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465456886,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465458613,"data":"       | Then y_A^2 = 169 - x_A^2 = 169 -25 =144 =\u003e y_A = 12 (positive). So A = (5,12). Good.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465460584,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465462328,"data":"       | Now M is midpoint of BC: B(0,0) C(14,0) =\u003e M = (7,0).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46546422,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465465884,"data":"       | Now circumcircle of triangle ABC. Compute its center O and radius R.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465467842,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465469558,"data":"       | We can compute using perpendicular bisectors. Let's compute with python sympy.assistantanalysisLet's compute O.assistantanalysis to=python codeimport sympy as sp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46547172,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465473478,"data":"       | # define points\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465475221,"data":"       | B = sp.Point(0,0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465476983,"data":"       | C = sp.Point(14,0)\n"}
