,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465528544,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465530295,"data":"       | Now line AP passes through M (7,0). So we need point P on circumcircle such that line through A (5,12) and M (7,0) intersects circumcircle at another point P (different from A). Since A is on circumcircle, the line AM intersect circle again at P.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465532702,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465534451,"data":"       | So we can find intersection of line AM with circumcircle besides A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465536392,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465538077,"data":"       | Parametric equation of line AM: passes through A and M. Compute intersection.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465539992,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465541643,"data":"       | Let's compute using sympy.assistantanalysis to=python codeimport sympy as sp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465543574,"data":"       | A = sp.Point(5,12)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.465545309,"data":"       | M = sp.Point(7,0)\n"}
