,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466202624,"data":"     - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46620459,"data":"     Libraries: import math | import sympy as sp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466206425,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466208061,"data":"     [Turn 1]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466209766,"data":"     [Reasoning] (2718 chars):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466211472,"data":"       | analysisWe need to solve geometry problem.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466213294,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.4662154,"data":"       | Given triangle ABC with sides 13-14-15. M is midpoint of BC. P is point on circumcircle such that M lies on line AP (i.e., AP passes through M). So P is second intersection of line through A and M with circumcircle (other than A). Then there is unique point Q on segment AM such that angle PBQ = angle PCQ. Q is on AM interior. Need AQ length expressed as m/√n (simplify). Find m+n.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466218294,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466220005,"data":"       | We need to compute geometry coordinates.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466221842,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466223558,"data":"       | Let's set up coordinates: easiest use triangle with known sides; 13-14-15 is scalene. Use coordinates: place B at (0,0), C at (14,0) (since BC=14). Then find coordinates of A using side lengths AB=13, AC=15.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466225836,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466227578,"data":"       | Let A = (x_A, y_A) with distance to B: sqrt(x_A^2 + y_A^2) = 13. Distance to C: sqrt((x_A-14)^2 + y_A^2) = 15.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466229572,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466231262,"data":"       | Solve for x_A, y_A. Subtract squares: (x_A-14)^2 + y_A^2 - (x_A^2 + y_A^2) = 15^2 - 13^2 = 225 - 169 = 56.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466233289,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466235044,"data":"       | Compute: (x_A^2 -28 x_A +196) + y_A^2 - x_A^2 - y_A^2 = -28 x_A +196 = 56 =\u003e -28 x_A = -140 =\u003e x_A = 5.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466237109,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46623883,"data":"       | Then AB distance: sqrt(5^2 + y_A^2) =13 =\u003e 25 + y_A^2 = 169 =\u003e y_A^2 =144 =\u003e y_A = sqrt(144)=12. Positive orientation choose y_A =12.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466241061,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466242751,"data":"       | Thus coordinates: A(5,12), B(0,0), C(14,0). Good.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466244666,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466246339,"data":"       | M is midpoint of BC: ((0+14)/2, (0+0)/2) = (7,0).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466248292,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46624997,"data":"       | Line AM: passes through A (5,12) and M (7,0). Find its equation; param t: point = A + t*(M-A). For t from 0 to 1 gives segment.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466252019,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466253737,"data":"       | Vector M-A = (7-5, 0-12) = (2, -12). So param: (x,y) = (5 + 2t, 12 -12t). When t=0 -\u003e A; t=1 -\u003e M.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466257016,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466258741,"data":"       | Find intersection of line AM with circumcircle of triangle ABC other than A: point P.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466262758,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466264536,"data":"       | First find circumcircle of triangle ABC. Compute circumcenter O and radius R.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466266465,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466268158,"data":"       | Given coordinates, we can compute using perpendicular bisectors.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466270044,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466271806,"data":"       | Better use sympy to compute.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466273563,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466275228,"data":"       | But we can also compute analytically. Let's compute O.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466277098,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466278805,"data":"       | We have triangle with B(0,0), C(14,0), A(5,12). Since BC is horizontal, its perpendicular bisector is vertical line x = 7. So O has x-coordinate 7.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466280952,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466283101,"data":"       | Now need O's y-coordinate: intersection of x=7 line with perpendicular bisector of AB (or AC). Let's compute midpoint of AB: ((5+0)/2, (12+0)/2) = (2.5,6). Slope of AB: (12-0)/(5-0) = 12/5 = 2.4. Perpendicular slope = -5/12.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466285537,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46628725,"data":"       | Equation of perpendicular bisector of AB: passes through (2.5,6) with slope -5/12. So y - 6 = (-5/12)(x - 2.5). Set x=7 to find O.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466289292,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466290967,"data":"       | Compute: y = 6 + (-5/12)*(7 - 2.5) = 6 - (5/12)*(4.5) = 6 - (5*4.5)/12 = 6 - (22.5)/12 = 6 - 1.875 = 4.125 = 33/8? Let's compute: 4.125 = 33/8 indeed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46629308,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466294757,"data":"       | Thus O = (7,33/8). Radius R = distance from O to B (or any vertex). Compute distance to B (0,0): sqrt((7)^2 + (33/8)^2). Compute.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466296808,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466298506,"data":"       | Let's compute in Python for exact rational.assistantanalysis to=python codeimport sympy as sp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466300478,"data":"       | x=sp.Rational\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46630222,"data":"       | R2 = (x(7)**2 + (x(33,8))**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466303995,"data":"       | R2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466305672,"data":"     [Code]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466307415,"data":"       | import sympy as sp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46630913,"data":"       | x=sp.Rational\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466310893,"data":"       | R2 = (x(7)**2 + (x(33,8))**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46631266,"data":"       | R2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466314316,"data":"     [Output]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466315995,"data":"       \u003e 4225/64\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466317694,"data":"       \u003e \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466319404,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46632099,"data":"     [Turn 2]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46632268,"data":"     [Reasoning] (718 chars):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466324614,"data":"       | analysisSo R^2 = 4225/64 =\u003e R = sqrt(4225)/8 = 65/8 (since 65^2=4225). So radius = 65/8 = 8.125.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466328605,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466330386,"data":"       | Check: distance O to A: compute: (5-7)^2 + (12-33/8)^2 = (-2)^2 + ( (96/8 -33/8)=63/8 )^2 = 4 + (63/8)^2 = 4 + 3969/64 = (256/64 + 3969/64) = 4225/64 same. Good.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466332542,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46633424,"data":"       | Now line AM: param as above. Intersection with circumcircle: solve for t such that point lies on circle (x-7)^2 + (y-33/8)^2 = (65/8)^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46633629,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466337978,"data":"       | We know t=0 gives point A (5,12) which is on circle. Need other intersection t ≠ 0. Solve quadratic; one root t=0, other t = something.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466340062,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466341824,"data":"       | Let's compute.assistantanalysis to=python codet=sp.symbols('t')\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466343834,"data":"       | x_expr=5+2*t\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466345612,"data":"       | y_expr=12-12*t\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466358574,"data":"       | eq = (x_expr-7)**2 + (y_expr-sp.Rational(33,8))**2 - (sp.Rational(65,8))**2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466360883,"data":"       | sp.expand(eq)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466362749,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466364538,"data":"     [Code]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466366371,"data":"       | t=sp.symbols('t')\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466368263,"data":"       | x_expr=5+2*t\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466370056,"data":"       | y_expr=12-12*t\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466371894,"data":"       | eq = (x_expr-7)**2 + (y_expr-sp.Rational(33,8))**2 - (sp.Rational(65,8))**2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466373885,"data":"       | sp.expand(eq)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466375684,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466377496,"data":"     [Output]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466379312,"data":"       \u003e 148*t**2 - 197*t\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466381203,"data":"       \u003e \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466383074,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466384747,"data":"     [Turn 3]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466386488,"data":"     [Reasoning] (301 chars):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466388789,"data":"       | analysisEquation simplifies to 148 t^2 - 197 t = t*(148 t - 197)=0. So t=0 (A) or t=197/148.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466390845,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466392612,"data":"       | Thus P corresponds to t = 197/148.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466394449,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466396203,"data":"       | Compute coordinates of P: (x,y) = (5+2t, 12-12t). Let's compute rational.assistantanalysis to=python codet_val=sp.Rational(197,148)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466398429,"data":"       | P = sp.Point(5+2*t_val, 12-12*t_val)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466400267,"data":"       | P\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466402016,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466403781,"data":"     [Code]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466405619,"data":"       | t_val=sp.Rational(197,148)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466409463,"data":"       | P = sp.Point(5+2*t_val, 12-12*t_val)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466411389,"data":"       | P\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466413107,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466414935,"data":"     [Output]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466416747,"data":"       \u003e Point2D(567/74, -147/37)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.466418577,"data":"       \u003e \n"}
