,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.467291201,"data":"       | Now find circumcenter O of triangle ABC and radius R. But we also need point P: intersection of line through A and M (midpoint of BC) with circumcircle (other than A). Because P is point on circumcircle such that M lies on AP. So line AP passes through M. Since M is midpoint of BC: B(0,0), C(14,0) =\u003e M = (7,0). Indeed M is on x-axis at (7,0). So we have line through A(5,12) and M(7,0). Compute its equation; find intersection with circumcircle other than A to get P.\n"}
