,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.46799308,"data":"       | Triangle ABC side lengths: AB=13, BC=14, CA=15. So it's scalene. Need M midpoint of BC. P is point on circumcircle such that M is on AP (i.e., line AP passes through M). There are two points on circle where line through A and M intersect the circumcircle: A itself and another point P (the second intersection). So P is the second intersection of line AM with circumcircle.\n"}
