,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.468011491,"data":"       | Let’s use coordinate geometry: Put B at (0,0), C at (14,0) (since BC=14). Then side lengths AB=13, AC=15.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.468013485,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.468015248,"data":"       | We need coordinates of A such that distances: |AB|=13, |AC|=15.\n"}
