,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4372.468214964,"data":"       | Given B and C are symmetric about vertical line x=7 (the perpendicular bisector of BC) but triangle is not symmetric because A not symmetric (actually A's x=5, not 7). However Q is on AM (which is not symmetric). This condition might uniquely determine Q.\n"}
