,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315443274,"data":"       | analysisWe need number of subsets of {1,...,10} that contain exactly one pair of consecutive integers. Means among all elements in subset, there is exactly one adjacent pair (i,i+1) present, and no other adjacent pairs. Also note that a subset could contain more than two elements; but only one pair of consecutive numbers appears. However, there could be longer runs? Example: {1,2,3} contains pairs (1,2) and (2,3) two pairs, so not allowed. So any run of length \u003e2 would contain multiple consecutive pairs, not allowed. So the subset must not contain any three consecutive numbers. It can contain at most one adjacent pair, and all other elements must be isolated (no adjacency to any other element). Also the pair itself cannot be adjacent to any other element (i.e., cannot have i-1 or i+2 also in subset) because that would create another consecutive pair. So the subset structure: choose a pair (i,i+1) where i from 1 to 9. Then we must choose any subset of the remaining numbers that does not contain any consecutive numbers, and also does not contain numbers adjacent to the chosen pair (i-1 and i+2) because those would create extra consecutive pairs. So we must exclude i-1 and i+2 from being selected. Also we must avoid any other consecutive pairs among the rest.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315448458,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315449636,"data":"       | Thus we need to count for each i, the number of subsets of the set S_i = {1,...,10} \\ {i,i+1,i-1,i+2} (where we treat out-of-range indices as not present) such that the subset contains no consecutive numbers (i.e., is an independent set in a path graph). Also note that the remaining numbers are split into two intervals: left side of i-1 (i.e., 1..i-2) and right side of i+3..10. Because we removed i-1 and i+2, the remaining numbers are separated into two blocks that are not adjacent across the gap. So we can count subsets with no consecutive numbers in each block independently, multiply.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315451922,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315452949,"data":"       | Thus for each i, we need number of subsets of a path of length L (size of block) with no adjacent elements. This is known to be F_{L+2} where F_n is Fibonacci numbers with F_1=1, F_2=1 (or F_0=0). Let's verify: Number of independent sets of path of n vertices = F_{n+2}. For n=0 (empty set) we have 1 = F_2 = 1. For n=1, subsets: {} and {v} =\u003e2 = F_3=2. For n=2, subsets: {},{1},{2} =\u003e3 = F_4=3. Works.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315454772,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315455794,"data":"       | Thus for each block length L, count = F_{L+2}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315457092,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315460184,"data":"       | Now we need to sum over i=1..9.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315461346,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315462371,"data":"       | Let's compute lengths.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315463471,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.31546453,"data":"       | Define left block length = i-2 (since numbers 1..i-2 are available). Right block length = 10 - (i+2) = 8 - i? Wait compute: numbers from i+3 to 10 inclusive. Count = 10 - (i+2) = 8 - i? Actually 10 - (i+2) = 8 - i? Let's test i=1: right block numbers from 4 to 10 =\u003e length 7. 8 - 1 =7 correct. i=9: right block numbers from 12? Actually i+3=12 \u003e10, so right block length 0. 8-9 = -1? Not correct. So formula only valid for i \u003c=8. For i=9, right block length = 0 because i+3=12 \u003e10. So we need piecewise.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315466659,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315467696,"data":"       | General: right block length = max(0, 10 - (i+2)). Equivalent to max(0, 8 - i). So for i \u003c=8, length = 8 - i. For i=9, length =0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315468997,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315470039,"data":"       | Similarly left block length = max(0, i-2). For i \u003e=2 else 0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315471228,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.315472253,"data":"       | Now compute for each i.\n"}
