,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.316175725,"data":"       | Thus the subset may include any other numbers as long as they are not adjacent to each other, and also they cannot be adjacent to the pair? Wait, they could be adjacent to one member of the pair, but that would create another consecutive pair. For example, subset {1,2,4} includes pair (1,2) only; 4 is not adjacent to 2 or 1, fine. But subset {1,2,3} includes pair (1,2) and (2,3) -\u003e two pairs, not allowed. So any other element cannot be adjacent to either member of the pair, because that would create another consecutive pair. Also cannot be adjacent to each other.\n"}
