,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.316180501,"data":"       | Thus we need to choose exactly one adjacent pair (i,i+1), and then choose a subset of the remaining numbers from the set {1..10} \\ {i,i+1} such that no two chosen numbers are consecutive, and also none of the chosen numbers are adjacent to i or i+1 (i.e., cannot be i-1 or i+2). However, note that i-1 and i+2 are already removed from the set? Actually they are not removed automatically; we need to ensure they are not selected. So effectively after fixing the pair (i,i+1), we cannot select i-1 or i+2, and also cannot select any other pair of consecutive numbers among the rest.\n"}
