,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.316588442,"data":"       | Both \\(k\\) and \\(k+1\\) are forced to be in the subset; all other\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.316589654,"data":"       | consecutive pairs must be avoided.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.316590693,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.316591663,"data":"       | Consequently we cannot also take the neighbours \\(k-1\\) and \\(k+2\\)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.316592879,"data":"       | (because they would create another consecutive pair).  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4400.316593944,"data":"       | Thus the remaining admissible elements are\n"}
