,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667828924,"data":"       | Let’s set u = sqrt(2a - a b), v = sqrt(2b - a b). Then u+v = k. Also u^2 = a(2 - b), v^2 = b(2 - a). Also note that u^2 + v^2 = a(2 - b) + b(2 - a) = 2a - a b + 2b - a b = 2(a+b) - 2ab = 2(a+b - a b). Not directly helpful.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66783042,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66783148,"data":"       | We also have product uv = sqrt{(2a - a b)(2b - a b)} = sqrt{ab (2 - b)(2 - a)}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66783268,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667833706,"data":"       | Maybe we can square equation: (u+v)^2 = u^2 + v^2 + 2uv = k^2.\n"}
