,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667958527,"data":"       | T=1 + p - q - p*q\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667959573,"data":"       | sp.expand(S*T)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66796061,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667961611,"data":"     [Code]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667962686,"data":"       | import sympy as sp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667963789,"data":"       | p,q=sp.symbols('p q')\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66796494,"data":"       | S=1 - p + q - p*q\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667965987,"data":"       | T=1 + p - q - p*q\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667967027,"data":"       | sp.expand(S*T)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66796808,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667969106,"data":"     [Output]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667970157,"data":"       \u003e p**2*q**2 - p**2 - q**2 + 1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667971274,"data":"       \u003e \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66797235,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667973354,"data":"     [Turn 2]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667974413,"data":"     [Reasoning] (2735 chars):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667975477,"data":"       | analysisGreat! S*T = 1 - p^2 - q^2 + p^2 q^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667976594,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667979561,"data":"       | Thus AB = sqrt(1 - p^2 - q^2 + p^2 q^2) = sqrt{(1 - p^2)(1 - q^2)}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66798074,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66798179,"data":"       | Because (1 - p^2)(1 - q^2) = 1 - p^2 - q^2 + p^2 q^2. Indeed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667982926,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667983939,"data":"       | Thus AB = sqrt{(1 - p^2)(1 - q^2)}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667985021,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667986024,"data":"       | Thus we have:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667987074,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667988089,"data":"       | sqrt{(1 - p^2)(1 - q^2)} = (k^2 - 2 + 2 p q)/2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66798922,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667990237,"data":"       | Thus we have relation:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667991311,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667992313,"data":"       | 2 sqrt{(1 - p^2)(1 - q^2)} = k^2 - 2 + 2 p q.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667993393,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.6679944,"data":"       | Rearrange:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667995424,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667996467,"data":"       | k^2 = 2 - 2 p q + 2 sqrt{(1 - p^2)(1 - q^2)}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66799754,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667998569,"data":"       | Thus\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.667999589,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66800059,"data":"       | k^2 = 2[1 - p q + sqrt{(1 - p^2)(1 - q^2)}].\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668001714,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66800276,"data":"       | Now note that k is given: for (p,q) pair, k = 1, sqrt2, sqrt3 respectively.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668003984,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668005013,"data":"       | Thus we have:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66800606,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.6680071,"data":"       | For (p,q): k1 = 1 =\u003e k1^2 = 1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668008224,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668009251,"data":"       | Thus 1 = 2[1 - p q + sqrt{(1 - p^2)(1 - q^2)}].\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668010357,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668011377,"data":"       | =\u003e Divide by 2: 0.5 = 1 - p q + sqrt{(1 - p^2)(1 - q^2)}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66801257,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66801357,"data":"       | Thus sqrt{(1 - p^2)(1 - q^2)} = p q - 0.5.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668014677,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668015697,"data":"       | Similarly for (q,r): k2 = sqrt2 =\u003e k2^2 = 2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668016846,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668017874,"data":"       | Thus 2 = 2[1 - q r + sqrt{(1 - q^2)(1 - r^2)}] =\u003e divide by 2: 1 = 1 - q r + sqrt{(1 - q^2)(1 - r^2)}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668019163,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668020314,"data":"       | Thus sqrt{(1 - q^2)(1 - r^2)} = q r.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668021424,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66802428,"data":"       | Similarly for (r,p): k3 = sqrt3 =\u003e k3^2 = 3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668025446,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668026563,"data":"       | Thus 3 = 2[1 - r p + sqrt{(1 - r^2)(1 - p^2)}] =\u003e divide by 2: 1.5 = 1 - r p + sqrt{(1 - r^2)(1 - p^2)}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668027784,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66802881,"data":"       | Thus sqrt{(1 - r^2)(1 - p^2)} = r p + 0.5.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668029913,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668030936,"data":"       | Thus we have three equations:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668032,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66803306,"data":"       | (1) sqrt{(1 - p^2)(1 - q^2)} = p q - 1/2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66803467,"data":"       | (2) sqrt{(1 - q^2)(1 - r^2)} = q r.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668035793,"data":"       | (3) sqrt{(1 - r^2)(1 - p^2)} = r p + 1/2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668037006,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668038029,"data":"       | Note that RHS must be nonnegative because sqrt nonnegative. So we need constraints.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66803939,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.6680404,"data":"       | Now we can square each equation to eliminate sqrt.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668041674,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668042691,"data":"       | Equation (1) squared:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668043886,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668044904,"data":"       | (1 - p^2)(1 - q^2) = (p q - 1/2)^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66804618,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668047181,"data":"       | Equation (2) squared:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66804835,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66804936,"data":"       | (1 - q^2)(1 - r^2) = (q r)^2 = q^2 r^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668050573,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668051573,"data":"       | Equation (3) squared:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668052727,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668053739,"data":"       | (1 - r^2)(1 - p^2) = (r p + 1/2)^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668054823,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668055827,"data":"       | Now we have three equations in p,q,r.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66805692,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66805799,"data":"       | Let’s denote a = p^2, b = q^2, c = r^2. Since p,q,r positive? Actually x,y,z positive, but p = 1 - x. Since x positive, p could be negative if x\u003e1. Not sure sign. However p,q,r may be positive or negative. But we have squares anyway.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668059504,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668060573,"data":"       | But also note that sqrt expressions involve (1 - p^2) etc. So we need |p| \u003c=1 for sqrt to be real (since 1 - p^2 \u003e=0). Similarly |q| \u003c=1, |r| \u003c=1. So p,q,r in [-1,1].\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66806215,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668063194,"data":"       | Now we have:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668064249,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66806531,"data":"       | (1 - a)(1 - b) = (sqrt(ab) - 1/2)^2? Wait p q = sqrt(ab) with sign? Since p,q could be negative, p q = sign(p q) sqrt(ab). But we can treat squares.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.6680685,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668069573,"data":"       | But maybe we can assume p,q,r \u003e=0? Let's test: Since x = 1 - p, and x positive, we need p \u003c 1. Also x \u003c=2 =\u003e p \u003e= -1. So p can be negative. But we also have constraints from equations.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668071096,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66807214,"data":"       | Let's attempt to solve system numerically to see values.assistantanalysis to=python codeimport sympy as sp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668073356,"data":"       | p,q,r = sp.symbols('p q r', real=True)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66807447,"data":"       | eq1 = (1-p**2)*(1-q**2) - (p*q - sp.Rational(1,2))**2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.6680756,"data":"       | eq2 = (1-q**2)*(1-r**2) - (q*r)**2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66807669,"data":"       | eq3 = (1-r**2)*(1-p**2) - (r*p + sp.Rational(1,2))**2\n"}
