,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66813039,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668131396,"data":"       | Thus p q r = (√2/2) * (1/4) = √2 / 8.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668132547,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.6681336,"data":"       | Thus product (p q r)^2 = ( (√2)/8 )^2 = 2 / 64 = 1/32.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668134747,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668135746,"data":"       | Thus ((1-x)(1-y)(1-z))^2 = (p q r)^2 = 1/32.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668136844,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668137876,"data":"       | Thus m/n = 1/32, relatively prime positive integers: m=1, n=32. Then m+n = 33.\n"}
