,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66827417,"data":"       | Assuming positive values (since angles between 0 and π/2), we have cos B cos C = sin B sin C =\u003e tan B = cot C =\u003e B + C = π/2 (90°). So B + C = 90°. Indeed 75° + 15° = 90°.\n"}
