,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.6686653,"data":"     [Reasoning] (5384 chars):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66866634,"data":"       | analysisWe have two possible sets:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668667536,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668668646,"data":"       | 1) α=π/6, β=π/4, γ=π/3 =\u003e A=π/8, B=π/24, C=5π/24.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668670044,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66867109,"data":"       | 2) α=5π/6, β=3π/4, γ=2π/3 =\u003e A=3π/8, B=11π/24, C=7π/24.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668672523,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668673667,"data":"       | Now we need to verify that these correspond to original equations with correct signs (since we used sin positive). Both sets have angles within (0, π/2). Indeed A=π/8 ≈22.5°, B≈7.5°, C≈37.5°. All \u003c90°, good.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668675403,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668676584,"data":"       | Second set: A=3π/8=67.5°, B≈82.5°, C≈52.5°. B=11π/24 ≈ 82.5°, still \u003c90°, okay.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66867803,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668679123,"data":"       | Now we need to compute x = a^2 = (√2 sin A)^2 = 2 sin^2 A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66868031,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668681326,"data":"       | Similarly y = 2 sin^2 B, z = 2 sin^2 C.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668682429,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668683436,"data":"       | Thus (1-x) = 1 - 2 sin^2 A = 1 - (1 - cos 2A) = cos 2A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668684577,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668685627,"data":"       | Because sin^2 A = (1 - cos 2A)/2, so 2 sin^2 A = 1 - cos 2A. Then 1 - x = 1 - (1 - cos 2A) = cos 2A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668686826,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668687854,"data":"       | Thus (1-x)(1-y)(1-z) = cos 2A * cos 2B * cos 2C.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66868895,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668689966,"data":"       | Therefore the quantity squared is (cos 2A cos 2B cos 2C)^2 = (cos 2A cos 2B cos 2C)^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668691167,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66869216,"data":"       | Now compute for each solution.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668693246,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668694249,"data":"       | First set: A=π/8 =\u003e 2A=π/4 =\u003e cos π/4 = √2/2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668695526,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668696543,"data":"       | B=π/24 =\u003e 2B=π/12 =\u003e cos π/12 = cos 15° = √6+√2 over 4? Actually cos 15° = (√6 + √2)/4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66869797,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668699006,"data":"       | C=5π/24 =\u003e 2C=5π/12 =\u003e cos 5π/12 = cos 75° = (√6 - √2)/4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668700284,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66870132,"data":"       | Thus product cos π/4 * cos π/12 * cos 5π/12 = (√2/2) * ((√6+√2)/4) * ((√6-√2)/4).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66870429,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668705604,"data":"       | Compute product: (√2/2) * (( (√6)^2 - (√2)^2 ) / 16 )? Because (a+b)(a-b)=a^2 - b^2. So ((√6+√2)(√6-√2) = 6 - 2 = 4). So product = (√2/2) * (4 / 16) = (√2/2) * (1/4) = √2 / 8.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66870717,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668708173,"data":"       | Thus product = √2/8. Square gives (2)/64 = 2/64 = 1/32. Indeed matches numeric.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668709374,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668710433,"data":"       | Second set: A=3π/8 =\u003e 2A=3π/4 =\u003e cos 3π/4 = -√2/2 (negative). B=11π/24 =\u003e 2B=11π/12 =\u003e cos 11π/12 = cos (π - π/12) = -cos π/12 = -(√6+√2)/4. C=7π/24 =\u003e 2C=7π/12 =\u003e cos 7π/12 = cos (π - 5π/12) = -cos 5π/12 = -(√6-√2)/4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668712414,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668713527,"data":"       | Product = (-√2/2) * (-(√6+√2)/4) * (-(√6-√2)/4) = (-)*( -)*( -) = - (since three negatives). So product = - (√2/2) * ((√6+√2)(√6-√2))/16 = - (√2/2) * (4)/16 = - (√2/2) * (1/4) = -√2/8. Square gives same 1/32.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668715129,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66871612,"data":"       | Thus both solutions give same squared product.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668717194,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668718233,"data":"       | Thus answer m+n = 1+32 = 33.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668719309,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66872031,"data":"       | Now we need to produce final answer.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668721387,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668722396,"data":"       | But we must present reasoning elegantly: transformation using substitution a = sqrt(2) sin A etc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668723576,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66872457,"data":"       | Let's craft final solution:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668725617,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668726663,"data":"       | Let x = 2 sin^2 A, etc. Show that sqrt(2x - xy) = sqrt{x(2-y)} = sqrt{2 sin^2 A * (2 - 2 sin^2 B)} = sqrt{2 sin^2 A * 2 cos^2 B} = 2 sin A cos B.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668727936,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66872898,"data":"       | Thus each equation becomes 2 sin A cos B + 2 sin B cos A = 2 sin(A+B) = constant. So we get sin(A+B) = 1/2, sin(B+C) = 1/√2, sin(C+A) = √3/2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668730313,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668731394,"data":"       | Thus A+B = π/6 or 5π/6 etc. Considering ranges (0,π/2) we get two possible sets, but both give same product.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668732684,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668733699,"data":"       | Compute (1-x) = 1 - 2 sin^2 A = cos 2A, etc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668734803,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668735804,"data":"       | Thus product = cos 2A cos 2B cos 2C = ±√2/8, square = 1/32.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668737003,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668738067,"data":"       | Thus answer 33.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668739114,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668741614,"data":"       | Now produce final answer.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668742721,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66874374,"data":"       | assistantfinal\\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66874485,"data":"       | \\begin{cases}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668745951,"data":"       | \\sqrt{2x-xy}+\\sqrt{2y-xy}=1\\\\[2mm]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668747216,"data":"       | \\sqrt{2y-yz}+\\sqrt{2z-yz}= \\sqrt2\\\\[2mm]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668748429,"data":"       | \\sqrt{2z-zx}+\\sqrt{2x-zx}= \\sqrt3\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66874955,"data":"       | \\end{cases}\\qquad (x,y,z\u003e0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668750694,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668751764,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668753074,"data":"       | --------------------------------------------------------------------\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668754241,"data":"       | ### 1.  A trigonometric substitution  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668755327,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668756324,"data":"       | Write  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66875742,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668758434,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668759487,"data":"       | x=2\\sin ^2A,\\qquad y=2\\sin ^2B,\\qquad z=2\\sin ^2C\\qquad (0\u003cA,B,C\u003c\\tfrac{\\pi}{2})\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668761011,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668762054,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668763074,"data":"       | because \\(0\u003cx,y,z\u003c2\\) is forced by the square‑roots.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668764427,"data":"       | Then  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668765504,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668766547,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668767607,"data":"       | \\sqrt{2x-xy}= \\sqrt{x(2-y)}= \\sqrt{2\\sin ^2A\\;2\\cos ^2B}=2\\sin A\\cos B,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66876901,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66877001,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66877108,"data":"       | \\sqrt{2y-xy}=2\\sin B\\cos A,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668772211,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668773224,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668774244,"data":"       | and similarly for the other two equations.  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66877537,"data":"       | Hence the system becomes  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668776434,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668777481,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668779307,"data":"       | \\begin{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668780374,"data":"       | 2\\sin A\\cos B+2\\sin B\\cos A \u0026=1,\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668781813,"data":"       | 2\\sin B\\cos C+2\\sin C\\cos B \u0026=\\sqrt2,\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668783113,"data":"       | 2\\sin C\\cos A+2\\sin A\\cos C \u0026=\\sqrt3 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668784431,"data":"       | \\end{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668785603,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668786811,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66878782,"data":"       | Using \\(\\sin u\\cos v+\\cos u\\sin v=\\sin(u+v)\\),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668790846,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668791867,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668793027,"data":"       | \\boxed{\\;\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668794127,"data":"       | \\begin{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668795333,"data":"       | \\sin (A+B)\u0026=\\tfrac12,\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668796546,"data":"       | \\sin (B+C)\u0026=\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt2},\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66879787,"data":"       | \\sin (C+A)\u0026=\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66879901,"data":"       | \\end{aligned}}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668800214,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668801226,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668802243,"data":"       | --------------------------------------------------------------------\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668803377,"data":"       | ### 2.  Determining the angles  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66880446,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66880551,"data":"       | Since each of \\(A,B,C\\) lies in \\((0,\\frac{\\pi}{2})\\), the possible\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668806847,"data":"       | values of the sums are  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668807914,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668808946,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66880996,"data":"       | A+B=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\ \\text{or}\\ \\frac{5\\pi}{6},\\qquad\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668811237,"data":"       | B+C=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\ \\text{or}\\ \\frac{3\\pi}{4},\\qquad\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66881252,"data":"       | C+A=\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\ \\text{or}\\ \\frac{2\\pi}{3}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668813684,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668814784,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66881583,"data":"       | Solving the linear system gives two admissible triples:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668817019,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668818024,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668819064,"data":"       | \\begin{array}{c|c|c}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668820154,"data":"       | \\text{choice}\u0026A\u0026B\u0026C\\\\ \\hline\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66882152,"data":"       | \\displaystyle\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{\\pi}{3}\u0026\\displaystyle\\frac{\\pi}{8}\u0026\\displaystyle\\frac{\\pi}{24}\u0026\\displaystyle\\frac{5\\pi}{24}\\\\[2mm]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668823454,"data":"       | \\displaystyle\\frac{5\\pi}{6},\\frac{3\\pi}{4},\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\u0026\\displaystyle\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\u0026\\displaystyle\\frac{11\\pi}{24}\u0026\\displaystyle\\frac{7\\pi}{24}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668825134,"data":"       | \\end{array}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66882617,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66882722,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668828216,"data":"       | Both satisfy \\(0\u003cA,B,C\u003c\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66882949,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668830514,"data":"       | --------------------------------------------------------------------\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668831696,"data":"       | ### 3.  Computing \\((1-x)(1-y)(1-z)\\)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668835186,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668836246,"data":"       | From \\(x=2\\sin ^2A\\),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668837397,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668838396,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66883942,"data":"       | 1-x = 1-2\\sin ^2A = \\cos 2A,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668840549,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66884156,"data":"       | and similarly \\(1-y=\\cos 2B,\\;1-z=\\cos 2C\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66884276,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66884376,"data":"       | Hence  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668844826,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668845834,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668846894,"data":"       | (1-x)(1-y)(1-z)=\\cos 2A\\cos 2B\\cos 2C .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668848124,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66884914,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668850147,"data":"       | For the first triple  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668851191,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668852207,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668853274,"data":"       | \\begin{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668854334,"data":"       | \\cos 2A \u0026=\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{4}= \\frac{\\sqrt2}{2},\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668855673,"data":"       | \\cos 2B \u0026=\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{12}= \\frac{\\sqrt6+\\sqrt2}{4},\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668857001,"data":"       | \\cos 2C \u0026=\\cos\\frac{5\\pi}{12}= \\frac{\\sqrt6-\\sqrt2}{4},\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668858287,"data":"       | \\end{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66885933,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66886033,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668861329,"data":"       | so  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668862383,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66886338,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668864386,"data":"       | \\cos 2A\\cos 2B\\cos 2C\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668865491,"data":"       |    =\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\cdot\\frac{4}{16}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668866694,"data":"       |    =\\frac{\\sqrt2}{8}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66886781,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66886881,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668869817,"data":"       | For the second triple each cosine is the negative of the above,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66887099,"data":"       | giving the product \\(-\\frac{\\sqrt2}{8}\\).  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668872217,"data":"       | In either case\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668873259,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668874253,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668875283,"data":"       | \\bigl[(1-x)(1-y)(1-z)\\bigr]^2=\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt2}{8}\\right)^2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668876579,"data":"       |                                  =\\frac{1}{32}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668877847,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668878874,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668881551,"data":"       | Thus  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66888273,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66888375,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668884763,"data":"       | \\frac{m}{n}= \\frac{1}{32},\\qquad m=1,\\;n=32,\\qquad m+n=33.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668886016,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668887017,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66888804,"data":"       | --------------------------------------------------------------------\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668889187,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668890287,"data":"       | \\boxed{33}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66889134,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668892353,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668893364,"data":"     - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - \n"}
