,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668896997,"data":"     Libraries: import itertools, sympy as sp, math, fractions, sys, itertools, sympy as sp | import sympy as sp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668898197,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66889918,"data":"     [Turn 1]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668900197,"data":"     [Reasoning] (1654 chars):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668901236,"data":"       | analysisWe need to solve system:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668902593,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668903589,"data":"       | sqrt(2x - x*y) + sqrt(2y - x*y) = 1   (1)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668904686,"data":"       | sqrt(2y - y*z) + sqrt(2z - y*z) = sqrt(2)   (2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.6689058,"data":"       | sqrt(2z - z*x) + sqrt(2x - z*x) = sqrt(3)   (3)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66890687,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.6689079,"data":"       | All variables positive reals.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668908957,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66891001,"data":"       | Goal: compute ((1-x)(1-y)(1-z))^2 = ((1-x)(1-y)(1-z))^2 = ((1-x)(1-y)(1-z))^2 rational? Provide m/n reduced; compute m+n.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66891126,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668912257,"data":"       | We need to solve system exactly perhaps yields rational numbers.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66891339,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668914426,"data":"       | Observation: expressions like sqrt(2x - xy) = sqrt(x(2 - y)). Similarly sqrt(2y - xy) = sqrt(y(2 - x)). So first equation: sqrt{x(2 - y)} + sqrt{y(2 - x)} = 1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66891574,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668916744,"data":"       | Second: sqrt{y(2 - z)} + sqrt{z(2 - y)} = sqrt{2}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668917854,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668918863,"data":"       | Third: sqrt{z(2 - x)} + sqrt{x(2 - z)} = sqrt{3}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668919967,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66892098,"data":"       | Thus we have symmetric-like system.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66892362,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66892465,"data":"       | Let’s denote a = sqrt{x(2 - y)}, b = sqrt{y(2 - x)}. Then a + b = 1. Also note that a^2 = x(2 - y), b^2 = y(2 - x). Multiply: a^2 b^2 = xy (2 - y)(2 - x). Might be helpful.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668926,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668927071,"data":"       | Similarly define c = sqrt{y(2 - z)}, d = sqrt{z(2 - y)} with c + d = sqrt{2}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668928404,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668929423,"data":"       | And e = sqrt{z(2 - x)}, f = sqrt{x(2 - z)} with e + f = sqrt{3}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66893067,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668931677,"data":"       | Observe relationships: a = sqrt{x(2 - y)}; f = sqrt{x(2 - z)}. Both involve sqrt{x} times something. Maybe we can express x in terms of a,b etc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668933133,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668934143,"data":"       | From a^2 = x(2 - y). b^2 = y(2 - x). Could solve for x,y.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66893538,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668936444,"data":"       | Let’s attempt to solve system using algebraic manipulation. Use sympy to solve for x,y,z rational? Let's attempt.assistantanalysis to=python codeimport sympy as sp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668937917,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668938916,"data":"       | x,y,z = sp.symbols('x y z', positive=True, real=True)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668940157,"data":"       | eq1 = sp.sqrt(x*(2-y)) + sp.sqrt(y*(2-x)) - 1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668941227,"data":"       | eq2 = sp.sqrt(y*(2-z)) + sp.sqrt(z*(2-y)) - sp.sqrt(2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668942457,"data":"       | eq3 = sp.sqrt(z*(2-x)) + sp.sqrt(x*(2-z)) - sp.sqrt(3)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66894359,"data":"       | sol = sp.nsolve((eq1, eq2, eq3), (x,y,z), (0.5,0.5,0.5))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668944936,"data":"       | sol\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.668945984,"data":"       | \n"}
