,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669230194,"data":"       | Case 1: A + B = π/6, B + C = π/4, A + C = π/3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66923139,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66923272,"data":"       | Solve linear system: Add first two: A + 2B + C = π/6 + π/4 = (2π+3π)/12 = 5π/12. But also A + C = π/3 = 4π/12. So subtract: (A+2B+C) - (A+C) = 2B = 5π/12 - 4π/12 = π/12 → B = π/24 ≈ 7.5°. Then A = π/6 - B = π/6 - π/24 = (4π-π)/24 = 3π/24 = π/8 = 22.5°. C = π/3 - A = π/3 - π/8 = (8π-3π)/24 = 5π/24 ≈ 37.5°. Check B + C = π/24 + 5π/24 = 6π/24 = π/4, matches. All angles are positive and less than π/2. So this set works.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669235104,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669236156,"data":"       | Thus (A,B,C) = (π/8, π/24, 5π/24). Check each \u003c π/2 yes.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669237417,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669238437,"data":"       | Now compute u = cos 2A = cos(π/4) = √2/2 ≈ 0.7071. Then x = 1 - u = 1 - √2/2 = (2 - √2)/2 ≈ 0.292893. Indeed matches numeric x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669239824,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669240853,"data":"       | Similarly v = cos 2B = cos(π/12) = cos 15° = √6+√2 over 4? Actually cos 15° = (√6 + √2)/4 ≈ 0.9659258. Then y = 1 - v = 1 - cos 15° = 1 - (√6+√2)/4 = (4 - √6 - √2)/4 ≈ 0.034074. Matches numeric.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66924243,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66924345,"data":"       | Similarly w = cos 2C = cos(5π/12) = cos 75° = (√6 - √2)/4 ≈ 0.258819. Then z = 1 - w = 1 - (√6 - √2)/4 = (4 - √6 + √2)/4 ≈ 0.7411809. Good.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669244916,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669245941,"data":"       | Thus we have exact expressions.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669247007,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669248004,"data":"       | Now compute (1 - x)(1 - y)(1 - z) = u * v * w = cos 2A * cos 2B * cos 2C.\n"}
