,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669560969,"data":"       | analysisTwo possible sets:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669562101,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669563137,"data":"       | 1) A=π/6, B=π/4, C=π/3 =\u003e α=π/8 (22.5°), β=π/24 (7.5°), γ=5π/24 (37.5°). All \u003cπ/2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669564657,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669566177,"data":"       | 2) A=5π/6, B=3π/4, C=2π/3 =\u003e α=3π/8 (67.5°), β=11π/24 (82.5°), γ=7π/24 (52.5°). But note β=11π/24 ≈ 82.5°, which is \u003eπ/2 (90°? Actually π/2 = 12π/24 = 90°, so 11π/24 = 82.5°, still less than π/2). So all still less than π/2? Let's check: α=3π/8 = 67.5°, \u003c 90°, ok. β=11π/24 = 82.5°, \u003c 90°, ok. γ=7π/24 = 52.5°, \u003c 90°, ok. So both sets satisfy positivity and \u003cπ/2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66956871,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669569897,"data":"       | But we also need that u = sqrt{2} sin α = sqrt{x} \u003e0; x = u^2 = 2 sin^2 α. Since α in (0,π/2), x in (0,2). Similarly for y,z.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669571267,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66957241,"data":"       | Both sets produce positive x,y,z.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669573487,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66957464,"data":"       | But we need to verify that original equations hold with these α,β,γ (they will because we derived them). However we also need to ensure that the square root expressions are real: need x(2 - y) \u003e=0 etc. Since x,y,z \u003c=2, and positive, 2 - y \u003e=0? Not necessarily; y could be \u003e2? But y = 2 sin^2 β \u003c=2. So 2 - y \u003e=0 always, okay.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669576529,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669577677,"data":"       | Thus both sets produce valid solutions. Are there multiple solutions? Possibly both produce same product (1-x)(1-y)(1-z) maybe? Let's compute.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669579003,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66958027,"data":"       | Compute x = 2 sin^2 α, y = 2 sin^2 β, z = 2 sin^2 γ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669581471,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669582637,"data":"       | We'll compute for both sets.assistantanalysis to=python codeimport sympy as sp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.6695854,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66958654,"data":"       | def compute(alpha,beta,gamma):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669587627,"data":"       |     x = 2*sp.sin(alpha)**2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66958883,"data":"       |     y = 2*sp.sin(beta)**2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669589881,"data":"       |     z = 2*sp.sin(gamma)**2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.66959096,"data":"       |     expr = ((1-x)*(1-y)*(1-z))**2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669592036,"data":"       |     expr_simpl = sp.simplify(expr)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669593114,"data":"       |     return sp.nsimplify(expr_simpl)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.669594223,"data":"       | \n"}
