,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670847768,"data":"     [Reasoning] (4376 chars):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67084882,"data":"       | analysisWe have two possible sets of S1,S2,S3 that satisfy positivity constraints.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670850021,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67085106,"data":"       | First set: S1 = π/6 (≈0.5236), S2 = π/4 (≈0.7854), S3 = π/3 (≈1.0472). Then α = (S1+S3 - S2)/2 = (π/6 + π/3 - π/4)/2 = compute symbolic: (π/6+π/3 = π/2) actually π/6 + π/3 = π/2 (since 1/6+1/3=1/2). Then subtract π/4: π/2 - π/4 = π/4. Divide by 2 =\u003e π/8 = 22.5°. Indeed α = π/8 ≈ 0.392699 rad.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670853083,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670854094,"data":"       | Beta = (S1+S2 - S3)/2 = (π/6+π/4 - π/3)/2. Compute: π/6+π/4 = (2π/12+3π/12)=5π/12. Subtract π/3 = 4π/12 =\u003e gives π/12. Divide by 2 =\u003e π/24 ≈ 0.1309 rad.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670855685,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670856717,"data":"       | Gamma = (S2+S3 - S1)/2 = (π/4 + π/3 - π/6)/2. Compute: π/4+π/3 = (3π/12+4π/12)=7π/12. Subtract π/6 = 2π/12 =\u003e 5π/12. Divide by 2 =\u003e 5π/24 ≈ 0.6545 rad.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670858293,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670859604,"data":"       | All are ≤ π/2 indeed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670860767,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67086183,"data":"       | Second set: S1 = 5π/6, S2 = 3π/4, S3 = 2π/3. Compute α = (5π/6+2π/3 - 3π/4)/2. Let's compute symbolic: 5π/6 = 10π/12; 2π/3 = 8π/12; sum = 18π/12 = 3π/2. Subtract 3π/4 = 9π/12 =\u003e 3π/2 - 3π/4 = (6π/4 - 3π/4) = 3π/4. Divide by 2 =\u003e 3π/8 ≈ 1.1781 rad (\u003cπ/2? Actually π/2 = 1.5708 rad, 3π/8 = 1.1781 rad yes). Beta = (5π/6+3π/4 - 2π/3)/2 = compute: 5π/6=10π/12, 3π/4=9π/12 sum=19π/12. Subtract 2π/3 = 8π/12 =\u003e 11π/12. Divide by 2 =\u003e 11π/24 ≈ 1.4399 rad (\u003cπ/2? Wait π/2=12π/24=0.5π = 12π/24 = 1.5708 rad. 11π/24 ≈ 1.4399 rad, okay). Gamma = (3π/4+2π/3 -5π/6)/2: compute 3π/4=9π/12, 2π/3=8π/12 sum=17π/12. Subtract 5π/6=10π/12 =\u003e 7π/12. Divide by 2 =\u003e 7π/24 ≈ 0.9163 rad (\u003cπ/2). So also valid.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670865507,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.6708665,"data":"       | Thus there are two solutions for α,β,γ (and thus for p,q,r). Which correspond to two possible sets of x,y,z.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670867737,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67086873,"data":"       | We need (1-x)(1-y)(1-z)^2? Actually ((1-x)(1-y)(1-z))^2. Since squares, both solutions may give same value (maybe). Let's compute.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67086999,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670870997,"data":"       | Recall p = sqrt{2} sin α, so x = p^2 = 2 sin^2 α = 2 (1 - cos 2α)/2 = 1 - cos 2α. Indeed x = 2 sin^2 α = 1 - cos 2α.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670872435,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670873437,"data":"       | Similarly y = 2 sin^2 β = 1 - cos 2β.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670876084,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670877143,"data":"       | z = 2 sin^2 γ = 1 - cos 2γ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67087826,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670879248,"data":"       | Thus 1 - x = 1 - (1 - cos 2α) = cos 2α.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670880368,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670881494,"data":"       | Similarly 1 - y = cos 2β, 1 - z = cos 2γ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670882723,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670883708,"data":"       | Thus (1 - x)(1 - y)(1 - z) = cos 2α cos 2β cos 2γ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670884894,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670885917,"data":"       | Then squared: (cos 2α cos 2β cos 2γ)^2 = (cos 2α cos 2β cos 2γ)^2 = (cos 2α cos 2β cos 2γ)^2 = product of squares.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67088724,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67088823,"data":"       | Thus we need compute (cos 2α cos 2β cos 2γ)^2 = (cos 2α cos 2β cos 2γ)^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670889444,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67089047,"data":"       | Thus we can compute cos 2α, cos 2β, cos 2γ using α,β,γ values for either solution.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67089176,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67089274,"data":"       | First solution: α = π/8, β = π/24, γ = 5π/24.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670893957,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670894945,"data":"       | Compute cos 2α = cos (π/4) = √2/2 = 1/√2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67089613,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670897344,"data":"       | cos 2β = cos (π/12) = cos 15°. cos 15° = √6 + √2 over 4? Actually cos 15° = (√6 + √2)/4 ≈ 0.9659.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670898745,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670899761,"data":"       | cos 2γ = cos (5π/12) = cos 75° = (√6 - √2)/4 ≈ 0.2588.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670901021,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670902064,"data":"       | Product: (1/√2) * ((√6 + √2)/4) * ((√6 - √2)/4). Multiply (√6 + √2)(√6 - √2) = (6 - 2) = 4. So product = (1/√2) * (4)/(16) = (1/√2) * (1/4) = 1/(4√2) = rationalizing maybe √2/8? Actually 1/(4√2) = √2/8.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670903743,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67090475,"data":"       | Thus cos 2α cos 2β cos 2γ = √2/8. Square it: (√2/8)^2 = 2/64 = 1/32.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670906003,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670907013,"data":"       | Thus ((1-x)(1-y)(1-z))^2 = 1/32.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670908073,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67090908,"data":"       | Second solution: α = 3π/8, β = 11π/24, γ = 7π/24.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67091029,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670911288,"data":"       | Compute cos 2α = cos (3π/4) = -√2/2 = -1/√2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670912484,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670913521,"data":"       | cos 2β = cos (11π/12) = cos (165°) = -cos 15° = -(√6 + √2)/4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670914781,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670915784,"data":"       | cos 2γ = cos (7π/12) = cos (105°) = -cos 75° = -(√6 - √2)/4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670918595,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670919647,"data":"       | Product: (-1/√2) * (-(√6 + √2)/4) * (-(√6 - √2)/4) = (-1/√2) * (positive? Let's compute signs: three negatives =\u003e negative overall. Multiply (-(√6 + √2)/4) * (-(√6 - √2)/4) = (+) ( (√6 + √2)(√6 - √2) ) /16 = 4/16 = 1/4. So product = (-1/√2) * (1/4) = -1/(4√2) = -√2/8.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67092157,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670922567,"data":"       | Thus cos product = -√2/8. Square =\u003e (√2/8)^2 = 1/32 again. So same result.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670923814,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670924818,"data":"       | Thus final answer: ((1-x)(1-y)(1-z))^2 = 1/32 = m/n with m=1, n=32 relatively prime.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670925983,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670926973,"data":"       | Thus m+n = 33.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67092802,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670929035,"data":"       | Check: Are there any other possible solutions? The positivity constraints allowed only those two combos. So answer is 33.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67093027,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.670931287,"data":"       | We should verify numerically solving original system to ensure x,y,z values correspond.\n"}
