,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.671322907,"data":"       | Then 1 - x = 1 - 2 sin^2 α = 1 - (1 - cos 2α)?? Since sin^2 α = (1 - cos 2α)/2. So 2 sin^2 α = 1 - cos 2α. Therefore 1 - x = 1 - (1 - cos 2α) = cos 2α.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67132581,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.671326881,"data":"       | Thus 1 - x = cos 2α, 1 - y = cos 2β, 1 - z = cos 2γ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.671328048,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.671329066,"data":"       | That's nice! So product (1-x)(1-y)(1-z) = cos 2α * cos 2β * cos 2γ.\n"}
