,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.671340316,"data":"       | Compute cos 2α = cos(π/4) = √2/2. cos 2β = cos(π/12) = cos 15° = √6+√2 /4? Actually cos 15° = (√6 + √2)/4. cos 2γ = cos(5π/12) = cos 75° = (√6 - √2)/4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.67134193,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.671343237,"data":"       | Thus product cos 2α cos 2β cos 2γ = (√2/2) * ((√6+√2)/4) * ((√6-√2)/4) = (√2/2) * (( (√6)^2 - (√2)^2 ) /16 )? Actually (a+b)(a-b) = a^2 - b^2. So ((√6+√2)(√6-√2)) = 6 - 2 = 4. So product = (√2/2) * (4/16) = (√2/2) * (1/4) = √2 /8.\n"}
