,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4452.671366833,"data":"       | Thus product = (-√2/2) * (-(√6+√2)/4) * (-(√6-√2)/4) = (-√2/2) * ((+?) Actually product of two negatives is positive, then times another negative gives negative. Let's compute: Two negatives -\u003e positive; positive * negative = negative. So overall sign negative.\n"}
