,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4482.930223853,"data":"       | Thus the maximum t such that r^{t-1} \u003c 10. Since r is integer \u003e1, we need to maximize t by choosing r as small as possible? Actually r is integer \u003e1, so r≥2. For r=2, we have 2^{t-1} \u003c 10 =\u003e t-1 ≤ floor(log_2 9.999...), log2(10) ≈ 3.3219. So t-1 ≤3 =\u003e t ≤4. So with r=2 we can have up to 4 terms (since 2^3=8\u003c10, 2^4=16\u003e10). So t=4 possible.\n"}
