,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4482.930791491,"data":"       | Observation: For a GP with ratio r\u003e1, terms grow exponentially. The number of terms that can stay within a factor of 10 (i.e., from lower bound to less than 10 times larger) is limited by r. Specifically, if we have terms a r^{n-1} for n = m,..., m+k-1, all must satisfy:\n"}
