,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4482.931198239,"data":"       | But we must ensure that there are no constraints from a being integer. For r=2, we can choose a=25? Actually we need a such that the terms with same digit length are not necessarily consecutive? But we can always choose a such that the first term that has d digits is a value X that is a power of r times a. Since a can be any positive integer, we can set a to be X (if we start with n=1). So choose a = X, r=2. Then the terms are X, 2X, 4X,... So we can achieve k=4.\n"}
