,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417034922,"data":"       | - RR (type R)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.41703601,"data":"       | - BB (type B)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417037204,"data":"       | - RB (type M) (mixed). But there are 2 orderings for mixed: RB and BR. So we need to treat them as two distinct states.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417038529,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417039609,"data":"       | Thus each pair has 1 state of RR, 1 state of BB, and 2 states of mixed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417040808,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417041948,"data":"       | Let’s define variables: Let a = number of RR pairs, b = number of BB pairs, c = number of mixed pairs (with order). Then a+b+c = 6, and c counts each mixed pair as 1 (but each mixed pair has 2 possibilities). The number of colorings for given a,b,c is: choose which pairs are RR (choose a from 6), then choose which of remaining are BB (choose b from 6-a), then the rest c are mixed. For each mixed pair, there are 2 orderings. So total colorings for given a,b is:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417043975,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417045142,"data":"       | N(a,b) = C(6, a) * C(6-a, b) * 2^{c}, where c = 6 - a - b.\n"}
