,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417304558,"data":"       | ### 1.  When can four vertices form a rectangle?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417305871,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417306951,"data":"       | A quadrilateral inscribed in a circle is a rectangle **iff** its two diagonals are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417308262,"data":"       | diameters (Thales’ theorem).  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417309466,"data":"       | Hence any rectangle whose vertices are among the 12 vertices must consist of\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417310816,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417311866,"data":"     - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - \n"}
