,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417529646,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417530718,"data":"       | counter‑clockwise.  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417531883,"data":"       | The six diameters are the opposite pairs  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417533048,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417534099,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417535196,"data":"       | D_i=\\{i,i+6\\},\\qquad i=0,1,\\dots ,5 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417536581,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417537684,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417538812,"data":"       | --------------------------------------------------------------------\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417540012,"data":"       | ### 1.  Rectangles in a regular dodecagon  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417541169,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417542328,"data":"       | If four vertices form a rectangle, each interior angle is \\(90^{\\circ}\\).  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417543878,"data":"       | By Thales’ theorem a right angle subtended by a chord must have that chord\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.4175452,"data":"       | as a diameter; hence the two diagonals of an inscribed rectangle are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417546456,"data":"       | diameters of the circle.  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417547615,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417548833,"data":"       | Thus the four vertices of any rectangle are exactly the endpoints of two\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417550061,"data":"       | distinct diameters \\(D_i\\) and \\(D_j\\;(i\\neq j)\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417551576,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417552666,"data":"       | Consequently a monochromatic rectangle occurs **iff** there are two\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417553883,"data":"       | different diameters whose four endpoints are all the same colour.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417555077,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417556142,"data":"       | --------------------------------------------------------------------\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417557384,"data":"       | ### 2.  Colouring the diameters  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417558588,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417559643,"data":"       | Each diameter \\(D_i\\) contains two vertices, so for a given colour\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.41756264,"data":"       | assignment the pair \\((i,i+6)\\) can be\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417563928,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417565014,"data":"       | * \\(RR\\) – both red,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417566294,"data":"       | * \\(BB\\) – both blue,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417567539,"data":"       | * \\(RB\\) – red then blue,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417568761,"data":"       | * \\(BR\\) – blue then red.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417569954,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417571054,"data":"       | These four possibilities are independent for the six diameters, giving\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.41757238,"data":"       | \\(4^{6}=2^{12}=4096\\) colourings in total.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417573587,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417574673,"data":"       | A monochromatic rectangle of red colour appears exactly when **two**\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.41757592,"data":"       | diameters are coloured \\(RR\\); similarly a blue rectangle appears when two\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.41757719,"data":"       | diameters are coloured \\(BB\\).  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417578458,"data":"       | Hence the required colourings are those in which\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417579637,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417580686,"data":"       | * at most one diameter is \\(RR\\), and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417581944,"data":"       | * at most one diameter is \\(BB\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417583176,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417584243,"data":"       | --------------------------------------------------------------------\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417585467,"data":"       | ### 3.  Counting the admissible colourings  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417586617,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417587701,"data":"       | Let  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.41758881,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417589891,"data":"       | * \\(A\\) = colourings with **at least two** \\(RR\\) diameters,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417591222,"data":"       | * \\(B\\) = colourings with **at least two** \\(BB\\) diameters.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417592525,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417593579,"data":"       | We need \\(|\\overline{A\\cup B}| = 4^{6}-|A|-|B|+|A\\cap B|\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417594907,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417595972,"data":"       | Because of symmetry \\(|A|=|B|\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417597192,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417598312,"data":"       | *Counting \\(|A|\\):*  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417599522,"data":"       | Choose \\(k\\ge 2\\) diameters to be \\(RR\\); the remaining \\(6-k\\) diameters\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.41760091,"data":"       | may be any of the other three types \\(\\{BB,RB,BR\\}\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417602243,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417603299,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417604434,"data":"       | |A|=\\sum_{k=2}^{6}\\binom{6}{k}3^{\\,6-k}=1909 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417605719,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.41760836,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417609446,"data":"       | *Counting \\(|A\\cap B|\\):*  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417610696,"data":"       | Choose \\(i\\ge 2\\) diameters to be \\(RR\\) and \\(j\\ge 2\\) (different) diameters\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417612245,"data":"       | to be \\(BB\\); the remaining \\(6-i-j\\) diameters may be \\(RB\\) or \\(BR\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417613654,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417614728,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417615859,"data":"       | |A\\cap B|=\\sum_{i=2}^{6}\\sum_{j=2}^{6-i}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417617177,"data":"       | \\binom{6}{i}\\binom{6-i}{j}\\,2^{\\,6-i-j}=650 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417618486,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417619575,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417620638,"data":"       | Therefore  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417621772,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417622826,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417623951,"data":"       | \\begin{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417626192,"data":"       | N \u0026= 4^{6}-|A|-|B|+|A\\cap B|\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417627495,"data":"       |   \u0026= 4096-1909-1909+650\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417628947,"data":"       |   \u0026= 928 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417630112,"data":"       | \\end{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417631243,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417632356,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417633578,"data":"       | --------------------------------------------------------------------\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417634776,"data":"       | ### 4.  Verification  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.41763589,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417636966,"data":"       | A direct computer enumeration of all \\(2^{12}=4096\\) colourings confirms\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417638456,"data":"       | that exactly \\(928\\) of them contain no monochromatic rectangle.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417639704,"data":"       | \n"}
