,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.41775541,"data":"       | So count total assignments with constraints.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417756549,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417757789,"data":"       | Let’s denote categories: a = number of RR pairs (0 or 1), b = number of BB pairs (0 or 1), c = number of mixed pairs (remaining). c = 6 - a - b. For each RR pair there is exactly 1 coloring (both red). For each BB pair 1 coloring. For each mixed pair there are 2 possibilities (RB or BR). So number of colorings for given (a,b) is:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417759501,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417760569,"data":"       | Choose which pairs are RR: choose a of 6 positions. Choose which of remaining are BB: choose b of remaining (6-a). Then the rest are mixed: each contributes factor 2^c.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417761989,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417763079,"data":"       | Thus count = sum_{a=0,1} sum_{b=0,1} C(6, a) * C(6-a, b) * 2^{6-a-b}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417764275,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417765326,"data":"       | Compute:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417766403,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417769038,"data":"       | Case a=0,b=0: choose none: C(6,0)=1, C(6,0)=1, factor 2^6 = 64.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417770291,"data":"       | \n"}
