,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417918329,"data":"       | We may also compute via inclusion-exclusion: total colorings 2^12 = 4096. Subtract those where there exists a monochromatic rectangle. Use counting of colorings with at least one red rectangle, etc. However our counting method using opposite pairs easier.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.417919888,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4511.41792104,"data":"       | Potential nuance: Are there rectangles where vertices are not consecutive opposite pairs but still rectangle? For example, choose vertices 0, 3, 6, 9 (every third). Those are also opposite pairs? Wait 0 opposite 6, 3 opposite 9. Yes they are two diameters, so rectangle. So our condition covers all.\n"}
