,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657005951,"data":"     [Reasoning] (2032 chars):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657007077,"data":"       | analysisWe need to solve for real numbers x\u003e1, y\u003e1 such that:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657008637,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657009719,"data":"       | log_x(y^x) = 10\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657010818,"data":"       | log_y(x^{4y}) = 10\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657011931,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657013141,"data":"       | Recall log base a of b = ln b / ln a.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657014437,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657015492,"data":"       | Thus:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.65701658,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657017651,"data":"       | ln(y^x)/ln x = 10 =\u003e (x ln y)/ln x = 10.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657018862,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657021025,"data":"       | Second: ln(x^{4y})/ln y = 10 =\u003e (4y ln x)/ln y = 10.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657023483,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657024504,"data":"       | Thus we have system:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657025593,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657026609,"data":"       | (1) x * ln y = 10 * ln x\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657027689,"data":"       | (2) 4y * ln x = 10 * ln y\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657028758,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657029769,"data":"       | We can treat unknowns x,y\u003e1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657030862,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657031894,"data":"       | Let’s denote A = ln x, B = ln y. Then x = e^A, y = e^B. Since x\u003e1 =\u003e A\u003e0, similarly B\u003e0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657033232,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657034244,"data":"       | Now rewrite equations:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.65703531,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657036315,"data":"       | (1) x * ln y = e^A * B = 10 * A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657037404,"data":"       | (2) 4y * ln x = 4 e^B * A = 10 * B.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657038484,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657039517,"data":"       | So we have:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657040547,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.65704153,"data":"       | e^A * B = 10 A   (eq1)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.65704262,"data":"       | 4 e^B * A = 10 B   (eq2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.65704367,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657044658,"data":"       | We need to solve for positive A,B.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657045712,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657046702,"data":"       | We can try to solve system.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657047754,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657048779,"data":"       | From eq1: B = 10 A / e^A. (1')\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657050014,"data":"       | From eq2: 4 e^B * A = 10 B =\u003e substitute B from (1') maybe.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657051222,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657052253,"data":"       | Alternatively solve for A in terms of B: From eq2: A = (10 B) / (4 e^B) = (5 B) / (2 e^B). (2')\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657053505,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657054535,"data":"       | Now substitute into (1'): B = 10 A / e^A = 10 * ((5 B)/(2 e^B)) / e^{A}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657055664,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657056664,"data":"       | But A depends on B; we need e^{A} also expressed in B.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657057787,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657058841,"data":"       | We have A = (5 B)/(2 e^B). So e^{A} = exp( (5 B)/(2 e^B) ). That's messy.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657060009,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657060993,"data":"       | Maybe better to eliminate A and B via ratio.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657062112,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657063123,"data":"       | Take eq1 and eq2:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657064165,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657065167,"data":"       | eq1: e^A B = 10 A\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.65706724,"data":"       | eq2: 4 e^B A = 10 B\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657068309,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657069376,"data":"       | Multiply both sides? Let's solve for A,B.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657070464,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657071474,"data":"       | From eq1: B/A = 10 / e^A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657072537,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657073541,"data":"       | From eq2: A/B = 10 / (4 e^B) = (5)/(2 e^B).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657074648,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657075634,"data":"       | Thus B/A = 2 e^B /5.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657076665,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657077687,"data":"       | Set equal:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657078712,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657079729,"data":"       | 10 / e^A = 2 e^B /5\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657080759,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657081779,"data":"       | =\u003e cross-multiply: 10*5 = 2 e^A e^B\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657082889,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657083946,"data":"       | =\u003e 50 = 2 e^{A+B}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657085182,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657086307,"data":"       | =\u003e e^{A+B} = 25\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657087437,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657088498,"data":"       | =\u003e A + B = ln 25 = ln(5^2) = 2 ln 5.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657089685,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657090735,"data":"       | Thus A + B = 2 ln 5.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657091824,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657092903,"data":"       | Now we can use relation B/A = 10 / e^A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.65709403,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657095139,"data":"       | But we also have e^A = x, e^B = y.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657096287,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657097341,"data":"       | We know A+B = 2 ln5.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657098429,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657099497,"data":"       | Now we can express B = 2 ln5 - A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657100621,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657101701,"data":"       | Plug into B/A = 10 / e^A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657102805,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657103893,"data":"       | So (2 ln5 - A)/A = 10 / e^A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657105005,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657106064,"data":"       | =\u003e (2 ln5)/A - 1 = 10 / e^A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657107242,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657108305,"data":"       | =\u003e (2 ln5)/A = 1 + 10 / e^A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657109464,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.65711053,"data":"       | =\u003e Multiply both sides by A: 2 ln5 = A + 10 A / e^A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657111793,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.6571129,"data":"       | =\u003e Rearranged: 2 ln5 = A (1 + 10 / e^A).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657115413,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657116521,"data":"       | We can solve for A numerically.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657117645,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657118732,"data":"       | Let’s use python to solve for A\u003e0.assistantanalysisassistantanalysis to=python codeimport mpmath as mp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657120081,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657121159,"data":"       | def f(A):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657122271,"data":"       |     return A*(1+10/mp.e**A) - 2*mp.log(5)\n"}
