,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657892968,"data":"       | analysisWe need to solve for positive real numbers x\u003e1, y\u003e1 such that:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657895988,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657897047,"data":"       | log_x(y^x) = 10\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657898087,"data":"       | log_y(x^{4y}) = 10\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657899131,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657900149,"data":"       | We need xy.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657901197,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657902223,"data":"       | Let’s translate.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657903287,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657904329,"data":"       | log base x of y^x = 10 means: (log(y^x) / log(x)) = 10 in natural logs. Equivalent: y^x = x^{10}. Wait careful: log_x(y^x) = 10 =\u003e x^{10} = y^x . Yes because a^{log_a b} = b. So y^x = x^{10}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657905722,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.65790676,"data":"       | Second: log_y(x^{4y}) = 10 =\u003e y^{10} = x^{4y}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657907902,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657908889,"data":"       | Thus we have system:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657909948,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657910951,"data":"       | (1) y^x = x^{10}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657911977,"data":"       | (2) x^{4y} = y^{10}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657913003,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657913976,"data":"       | We need x\u003e1,y\u003e1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657915065,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.65791608,"data":"       | Goal: find xy.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.6579171,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657918149,"data":"       | Let’s take logs maybe. Let’s set a = ln x, b = ln y. Then x = e^a, y = e^b. a,b\u003e0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657919372,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657920444,"data":"       | Equation (1): y^x = e^{b * x} = e^{b e^{a}} = x^{10} = e^{10 a}. So b e^{a} = 10 a. (since exponent equality: exponent both sides: b e^{a} = 10 a). Indeed because e^{b e^{a}} = e^{10 a}. So b e^{a} = 10 a. (Equation A)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657921847,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657922879,"data":"       | Equation (2): x^{4y} = e^{4y a} = e^{4 e^{b} a} = y^{10} = e^{10 b}. So 4 a e^{b} = 10 b. (Equation B)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657924092,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657925085,"data":"       | Thus we have:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657926105,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657927126,"data":"       | b e^{a} = 10 a   (1')\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.65792821,"data":"       | 4 a e^{b} = 10 b   (2')\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657929263,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657930276,"data":"       | We need xy = e^{a+b}. So we need a+b.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657931345,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657932359,"data":"       | We have two equations in a,b.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657933446,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657934429,"data":"       | Let’s solve.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.65793551,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657937596,"data":"       | From (1'): b = 10 a e^{-a}. From (2'): 4 a e^{b} = 10 b =\u003e substitute b expression.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657938818,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.65793995,"data":"       | Compute: 4 a e^{b} = 10 b = 10 * (10 a e^{-a}) = 100 a e^{-a}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657941078,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.657942115,"data":"       | Divide both sides by a (a\u003e0). 4 e^{b} = 100 e^{-a} =\u003e e^{b} = 25 e^{-a}. So b = ln 25 - a.\n"}
