,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658698488,"data":"       | (1) x ln y = 10 ln x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658699608,"data":"       | (2) 4y ln x = 10 ln y.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658700699,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658701769,"data":"       | We need xy.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658702995,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658704086,"data":"       | Let’s denote A = ln x, B = ln y. Since x\u003e1,y\u003e1, A\u003e0, B\u003e0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658705451,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658706544,"data":"       | Equation (1): x ln y = 10 ln x → (e^{A}) * B = 10 * A → e^{A} B = 10 A. (since x = e^{A})\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658707887,"data":"       | Equation (2): 4 y ln x = 10 ln y → 4 * e^{B} * A = 10 * B → 4 e^{B} A = 10 B.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658709226,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658710335,"data":"       | Thus we have two equations:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658712509,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658713798,"data":"       | (1) e^{A} B = 10 A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658714911,"data":"       | (2) 4 e^{B} A = 10 B.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658716138,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658717209,"data":"       | We can solve for A,B.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658718339,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658719438,"data":"       | From (1): B = 10 A e^{-A}. From (2): 4 e^{B} A = 10 B → substitute B.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658720686,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658721749,"data":"       | Compute: 4 e^{B} A = 10 B → divide both sides by A (A\u003e0): 4 e^{B} = 10 B / A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658723037,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658724115,"data":"       | But B/A =? Using B = 10 A e^{-A} =\u003e B/A = 10 e^{-A}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658725353,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658726436,"data":"       | Plug: RHS = 10 * (B/A) = 10 * 10 e^{-A} = 100 e^{-A}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658727622,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658728693,"data":"       | Thus we have: 4 e^{B} = 100 e^{-A} → e^{B} = 25 e^{-A} → taking ln: B = ln 25 - A.\n"}
