,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4611.658960054,"data":"       | analysisOnly one sign change; so unique root \u003e0. Also as A→0+, g(A) ≈ 0 + 0 - ln25 negative (since ln25~3.2189). At large A, term 10 A e^{-A} →0, g(A) ≈ A - ln25 → positive for A\u003eln25. So there is exactly one root. So unique positive solution.\n"}
