,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.861749402,"data":"       | Plug x = α: compute left side: x^2 f(x) + f(1 - x). With f(x) = 1 - x^2, we have x^2 (1 - x^2) + (1 - (1 - x)^2) = x^2 - x^4 + 1 - (1 - 2x + x^2) = x^2 - x^4 + 1 - 1 + 2x - x^2 = -x^4 + 2x. Indeed works for all x, because we derived from functional equation.\n"}
