,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.861767272,"data":"       | We have two equations in two unknowns f(a), f(b). Determinant zero, meaning the two equations are linearly dependent, so there is only one independent equation, giving infinite solutions (one degree of freedom). So indeed f(a) and f(b) are not uniquely determined; they can vary as long as they satisfy that single equation.\n"}
