,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862125139,"data":"       | But we should double-check that at those points the functional equation does not uniquely determine f(x). Let's compute for x = α: D=0, meaning coefficient matrix singular. Then there may be either no solution or infinite solutions. But the original functional equation alone (single equation) may still give some relation between f(x) and f(1 - x). However we might be able to solve for f(1 - x) in terms of f(x) etc. But uniqueness may fail because we have only one equation for two unknowns.\n"}
