,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862529139,"data":"       | analysisWe need to solve functional equation: x^2 f(x) + f(1 - x) = -x^4 + 2x for all real x. We need to find f(x) uniquely determined for all x except possibly at two points α and β where equation does not determine f uniquely. Compute α^2 + β^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862530786,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862531926,"data":"       | We have one functional equation linking f at x and at 1 - x. This is like a system of two equations for f(x) and f(1 - x). If we substitute x replaced by 1 - x, we get:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862533305,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.86253438,"data":"       | (1 - x)^2 f(1 - x) + f(x) = -(1 - x)^4 + 2(1 - x).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862537038,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862538169,"data":"       | Now we have linear system:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862539312,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862540395,"data":"       | Equation (A): x^2 f(x) + f(1 - x) = -x^4 + 2x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862541579,"data":"       | Equation (B): (1 - x)^2 f(1 - x) + f(x) = -(1 - x)^4 + 2(1 - x).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862542852,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862543949,"data":"       | We can solve for f(x) and f(1 - x) unless the coefficient matrix is singular.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862545189,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862546263,"data":"       | Write system in matrix form:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862547435,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862548509,"data":"       | [ x^2 , 1 ] [f(x)] = RHS1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862549635,"data":"       | [ 1 , (1 - x)^2 ] [f(1 - x)] = RHS2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862550789,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862551902,"data":"       | But careful: second equation is f(x) + (1 - x)^2 f(1 - x) = RHS2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862553116,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.86255419,"data":"       | Thus matrix M = [[x^2, 1], [1, (1 - x)^2]].\n"}
