,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862576022,"data":"       | Solve x - x^2 = -1 =\u003e -x^2 + x + 1 = 0 =\u003e x^2 - x - 1 = 0 =\u003e solutions x = (1 ± sqrt(1 + 4))/2 = (1 ± sqrt5)/2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862578992,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862580123,"data":"       | Thus D = 0 for x = (1 ± sqrt5)/2. Let's denote α = (1 + sqrt5)/2, β = (1 - sqrt5)/2. Or the other way, but they are two real numbers.\n"}
