,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.862592865,"data":"       | We can compute using formula: For two numbers that are roots of quadratic x^2 - x - 1 = 0 (since they satisfy that), we have sum S = α + β = 1 (coefficient -(-1)?? Wait: For quadratic x^2 - x - 1 = 0, sum of roots = 1, product = -1. Indeed, α + β = 1, αβ = -1.\n"}
