,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.863041176,"data":"       | analysisSympy solved with determinant not zero? Wait the solution yields f(x) = 1 - x^2, and f(1 - x) = -x^2 + 2x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.863042496,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.86304359,"data":"       | Check if this solution satisfies the equation for all x? Let's test.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.863044802,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.863046119,"data":"       | Plug f(x)=1 - x^2 into original: LHS = x^2*(1 - x^2) + f(1 - x) = x^2 - x^4 + f(1 - x). Need f(1 - x). If we compute using formula f(y) = 1 - y^2, then f(1 - x) = 1 - (1 - x)^2 = 1 - (1 -2x + x^2) = 2x - x^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.863047567,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.863048657,"data":"       | Thus LHS = x^2 - x^4 + (2x - x^2) = -x^4 + 2x, which matches RHS. Good! So f(x) = 1 - x^2 works for all x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.863049936,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.863051035,"data":"       | But note that at points where determinant zero, we might have infinite solutions (maybe any f values satisfy equation because both equations coincide). Let's test for x such that D=0: x = (1 ± sqrt5)/2. For such x, does the original functional equation alone give any restriction? Let's plug x into original: x^2 f(x) + f(1 - x) = -x^4 + 2x. That's one equation in two unknowns f(x) and f(1 - x). So not uniquely determined. Indeed there is infinite possibilities.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.863053106,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.863054192,"data":"       | Thus α and β are as above. Compute α^2 + β^2 = 3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.863055462,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.86305655,"data":"       | Let's double-check using numeric.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.863057724,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4635.863058846,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codeimport sympy as sp, math\n"}
