,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4675.026543867,"data":"       | Let's define: Suppose we have vertices A, B, C, D in order (counterclockwise). Then vectors: AB + AD = AC? Not exactly. But property: A + C = B + D (midpoint of diagonals same). So given three vertices, we can assign them to A, B, C (maybe not in order) and compute D accordingly.\n"}
