,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4696.968789504,"data":"       | analysisWe need to parse problem: Aya walks 9 km walk and then coffee shop. The total time includes walking time plus coffee shop time t minutes. When walking speed s km/h, total time = 4 hours (including coffee shop). So walking time = 4 hours - t minutes (converted to hours). Similarly, at speed s+2 km/h, total time = 2 hours 24 minutes = 2 + 24/60 = 2.4 hours, including same coffee shop time t minutes. So walking time = 2.4 - t (hours). Walking distance is 9 km. So we have equations:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4696.968791878,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4696.968793152,"data":"       | 9 / s = 4 - t/60   (1)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4696.968794385,"data":"       | 9 / (s+2) = 2.4 - t/60   (2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4696.968795652,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4696.968797004,"data":"       | We need to solve for s and t. Then compute total time when speed = s + 0.5 km/h: total time = walking time + coffee shop time = 9 / (s+0.5) + t/60 (hours). Convert to minutes.\n"}
