,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4696.969399844,"data":"       | Aya walks a 9-kilometer-long walk and stops at a coffee shop afterwards. She walks at constant speed s km/h, the walk takes her 4 hours, including t minutes spent in the coffee shop. When she walks at speed s+2 km/h, the walk takes her 2 hours 24 minutes (i.e., 2.4 hours? Let's compute: 2 hours 24 minutes = 2 + 24/60 = 2.4 hours) including same t minutes spent in coffee shop.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4696.969401672,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4696.969403037,"data":"       | We need to find total time (including t) when she walks at speed s+0.5 km/h. Output number of minutes (total time). So need t and s.\n"}
