,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311679778,"data":"       | analysisWe need to find (a+4)(b+4)(c+4) given three equations for (a+1)(b+1)(c+1)=1, (a+2)(b+2)(c+2)=2, (a+3)(b+3)(c+3)=3. a,b,c are complex numbers (roots unknown). We can treat variables x_i = a,b,c. The product of (x+ k) for k=1,2,3 known. We need product for k=4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311682929,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311697451,"data":"       | Let’s define polynomial P(t) = (t - a)(t - b)(t - c) = t^3 - s1 t^2 + s2 t - s3 where s1 = a+b+c, s2 = ab+bc+ca, s3 = abc.\n"}
