,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311702899,"data":"       | But (a + k)(b + k)(c + k) = ?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311704056,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311705173,"data":"       | We can express in terms of elementary symmetric sums: For any k, (a + k)(b + k)(c + k) = (k)^3 + s1 k^2 + s2 k + s3? Wait compute:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311706543,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311707795,"data":"       | Let’s consider polynomial Q(k) = (a + k)(b + k)(c + k). Expand: (k + a)(k + b)(k + c) = (k^3) + (a+b+c) k^2 + (ab+bc+ca) k + abc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311709187,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311710388,"data":"       | Yes because product of (k + a) = k^3 + (a+b+c)k^2 + (ab+bc+ca)k + abc.\n"}
