,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311712751,"data":"       | Thus Q(k) = k^3 + s1 k^2 + s2 k + s3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311713988,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.31171521,"data":"       | Given Q(1)=1, Q(2)=2, Q(3)=3. Need Q(4)=?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311716378,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311718728,"data":"       | Thus we have cubic polynomial Q(k) = k^3 + s1 k^2 + s2 k + s3 that passes through (1,1), (2,2), (3,3). Determine Q(4). Since Q(k) - k is a cubic minus linear? Let's define R(k) = Q(k) - k = k^3 + s1 k^2 + s2 k + s3 - k = k^3 + s1 k^2 + (s2 -1) k + s3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311720331,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311721529,"data":"       | We know R(1)=0, R(2)=0, R(3)=0 because Q(k)=k at those points. So R(k) is a cubic with roots 1,2,3. So R(k) = A (k-1)(k-2)(k-3) for some constant A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311722904,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311724054,"data":"       | Thus Q(k) = k + A (k-1)(k-2)(k-3).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311725243,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.31172646,"data":"       | Now we can compute Q(4) = 4 + A (4-1)(4-2)(4-3) = 4 + A * 3*2*1 = 4 + 6A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311727738,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311729931,"data":"       | We need to find A. Use any known value, say Q(1) = 1. Plug k=1: Q(1) = 1 + A (0) = 1 =\u003e holds for any A. Similarly for k=2,3 also hold because factor zero. So A is not determined by those three points! Indeed we have infinite possibilities: any cubic of form k + A(k-1)(k-2)(k-3) matches the three points. So we need extra condition from definition of Q(k) = k^3 + s1 k^2 + s2 k + s3. That imposes that the coefficient of k^3 is 1 (already). Let's expand Q(k) expression: Q(k) = k + A(k-1)(k-2)(k-3). Expand (k-1)(k-2)(k-3) = ?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.31173257,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.31173381,"data":"       | Compute: (k-1)(k-2) = k^2 -3k +2. Multiply by (k-3): (k^2 -3k +2)(k-3) = k^3 -3k^2 -3k^2 +9k +2k -6 = k^3 -6k^2 +11k -6.\n"}
