,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311759749,"data":"       | Thus indeed A is forced to be 1 by coefficient of k^3. So Q(k) = k + (k-1)(k-2)(k-3). Let's verify: Q(k) = k + (k-1)(k-2)(k-3) = k + (k^3 -6k^2 +11k -6) = k^3 -6k^2 +12k -6.\n"}
