,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311788709,"data":"       | analysisWe need to find (a+4)(b+4)(c+4) given three equations for (a+1)(b+1)(c+1)=1, (a+2)(b+2)(c+2)=2, (a+3)(b+3)(c+3)=3. a,b,c are complex numbers, presumably there are multiple solutions but the product (a+4)(b+4)(c+4) is uniquely determined.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311790237,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.31179145,"data":"       | We can treat variables x_i = a + i, y_i = b + i, z_i = c + i? Actually we have three unknowns a,b,c, and we have three equations of degree 3 each. The product of shifted variables at each shift i = 1,2,3 is given. We need product at shift 4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311793097,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311794206,"data":"       | We can think of polynomial P(t) = (t - a)(t - b)(t - c) = t^3 - S1 t^2 + S2 t - S3, where S1 = a+b+c, S2 = ab+bc+ca, S3 = abc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311795548,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311797144,"data":"       | But we have values of (a + k)(b + k)(c + k) = product of (k + a) etc = evaluate at t = -k? Wait (a + k) = a - (-k). So (a + k)(b + k)(c + k) = (-1)^3 * ( -a - k? Not helpful). Actually consider Q(k) = (a + k)(b + k)(c + k). This is a cubic polynomial in k: Q(k) = (k + a)(k + b)(k + c) = k^3 + (a+b+c) k^2 + (ab+bc+ca) k + abc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311798995,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311800071,"data":"       | Thus Q(k) = k^3 + S1 k^2 + S2 k + S3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311801211,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311802316,"data":"       | We are given Q(1)=1, Q(2)=2, Q(3)=3. Need Q(4)=?.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311803621,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311804743,"data":"       | Thus we have cubic polynomial Q(k) with known values at three points; we can find its coefficients or directly compute Q(4) using Lagrange interpolation.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311806123,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.31180721,"data":"       | Let’s denote unknown coefficients: Q(k) = k^3 + p k^2 + q k + r, where p=S1, q=S2, r=S3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311808488,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311809581,"data":"       | Given Q(1)=1 =\u003e 1 + p + q + r = 1 =\u003e p + q + r = 0. (Equation A)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311810955,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.31181208,"data":"       | Q(2)=2 =\u003e 8 + 4p + 2q + r = 2 =\u003e 4p + 2q + r = 2 - 8 = -6 =\u003e 4p + 2q + r = -6. (Equation B)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311813476,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311814557,"data":"       | Q(3)=3 =\u003e 27 + 9p + 3q + r = 3 =\u003e 9p + 3q + r = 3 - 27 = -24 =\u003e 9p + 3q + r = -24. (Equation C)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311815957,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311817066,"data":"       | We can solve for p,q,r.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311818244,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311820998,"data":"       | Subtract A from B: (4p+2q+r) - (p+q+r) = -6 - 0 =\u003e 3p + q = -6. (Equation D)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311822369,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311823487,"data":"       | Subtract B from C: (9p+3q+r) - (4p+2q+r) = -24 - (-6) = -18 =\u003e 5p + q = -18. (Equation E)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311824816,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311825916,"data":"       | Subtract D from E: (5p+q) - (3p+q) = -18 - (-6) =\u003e 2p = -12 =\u003e p = -6.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311827204,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311828318,"data":"       | Plug into D: 3(-6) + q = -6 =\u003e -18 + q = -6 =\u003e q = 12.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311829596,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311830678,"data":"       | Plug into A: p + q + r = 0 =\u003e -6 + 12 + r = 0 =\u003e r = -6.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311831991,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4713.311833078,"data":"       | Thus Q(k) = k^3 - 6 k^2 + 12 k - 6.\n"}
